      <text xml:space="preserve">{{Infobox_Film  |
  name     = Father of the Bride |
  image          = Fotb1950.jpg |
  imdb_id       = 0042451|
  producer         = [[Pandro S. Berman]] |
  director       = [[Vincente Minnelli]] |
  writer         = [[Edward Streeter]] (novel)&lt;br&gt;[[Frances Goodrich]]&lt;br&gt;[[Albert Hackett]] (screenplay) |
  starring       = [[Spencer Tracy]]&lt;br&gt;[[Joan Bennett]]&lt;br&gt;[[Elizabeth Taylor]] |
  music         = [[Adolph Deutsch]] |
  cinematography = [[John Alton]] |
  editing         = [[Ferris Webster]] |
  distributor    = [[Metro-Goldwyn-Mayer|MGM]]  |
  released   = [[June 16]], [[1950]] |
  runtime        = 92 min. |
  language = [[English language|English]] |
}}

'''''Father of the Bride''''' is a [[1950]] comedy film which tells the story of a man trying to cope with all of the disasters that happen along the way from the time that his daughter announces that she's engaged, until the wedding actually occurs.  It stars [[Spencer Tracy]] (Stan), [[Joan Bennett]] (Ellie), [[Elizabeth Taylor]] (Kay), [[Don Taylor]] (Buckley), [[Billie Burke]] and [[Leo G. Carroll]].

The movie was adapted by [[Frances Goodrich]] and [[Albert Hackett]] from the novel by [[Edward Streeter]].  It was directed by [[Vincente Minnelli]].

It was nominated for [[Academy Awards]] for [[Academy Award for Best Actor|Best Actor in a Leading Role]], [[Academy Award for Best Picture|Best Picture]] and [[Academy Award for Writing Adapted Screenplay|Best Writing, Screenplay]].

Father of the Bride had a sequel called ''[[Father's Little Dividend]]'' that was released in [[1951]]. In this film, Taylor's character has a baby.

Father of the Bride was also made into a [[Father of the Bride (TV series)|television series]] which aired on [[CBS]] during the 1961-62 season.  The cast included [[Leon Ames]] (Stan), [[Ruth Warrick]] (Ellie), and [[Myrna Fahey]] (Kay). 

A [[remake]] [[Father of the Bride (1991 film)|of the same name]] starring [[Steve Martin]] and [[Diane Keaton]] was released in [[1991]]. It had a [[Father of the Bride Part II|numeraled]] [[sequel]] in [[1995]], also starring Martin and Keaton. Just like the original's sequel, the daughter had a baby in the sequel to the remake. In this one, however, the mother of the bride had another child as well.

==External links==
