      <comment>new orleans ref</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Elysian Fields''' can refer to:

* [[Hoboken, New Jersey]] park, '''[[Elysian Fields, Hoboken, New Jersey|Elysian Fields]]''' where first [[Baseball]] game between clubs is believed to have been played in [[1846]]
* '''Elysian Fields''', an avenue in [[New Orleans]], and the setting of the [[novel]] [[A Streetcar Named Desire]]
* The [[New York]] band '''[[Elysian Fields (band)|Elysian Fields]]'''
* '''[[Elysium]]''', a section of [[Hades]] from [[Greek Mythology]]
* A song by the [[thrash metal]] band [[Megadeth]].
* The title track of the 2003 E.P. from [[CCM]] [[Hard Rock]] band [[Least Among Us]].

