    <title>Empusa</title>
    <id>80957</id>
    <revision>
      <id>40261186</id>
      <timestamp>2006-02-19T08:40:47Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <ip>194.149.100.146</ip>
      </contributor>
      <comment>cs:</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">''See also [[Empusa (disambiguation)]]''

In ancient [[Greek mythology]], the '''Empusa''' (or '''Empousa''') was a female supernatural [[monster]] or [[demon]]ess.  [[Hecate]] sent Empusa to harass travelers. It scared to death or ate anybody that travelled along the paths or roads it inhabited. The empusae are sometimes described as having [[donkey]]-like features.

More recent Greek tales describe the creature as a merely frightening [[shapeshifter]], but blame it for injuring sheep.

The Empusae are similar to the [[lilim]], and the legend of the former may be derived from that of the latter.  See also [[Lamia (mythology)|Lamia]].

