        <id>837482</id>
      </contributor>
      <text xml:space="preserve">In [[Greek mythology]], '''Epaphus''', also called '''Apis''', is the son of [[Zeus]] and [[Io (mythology)|Io]]. Epaphus is mostly known for founding the city of [[Memphis, Egypt]].  With his wife, named [[Memphis (mythology)|Memphis]], he had one daughter: [[Libya (mythology)|Libya]]. Hera (the wife and sister of Zeus) of was jealous of Zeus so she took him and eventually Io found Epaphus and they lived in Egypt where he founded the city of Memphis and then became Memphis' king.


[[Category:Greek mythological people]]
