  <page>
    <title>Iphicles</title>
    <id>80998</id>
    <revision>
      <id>35152129</id>
      <timestamp>2006-01-14T15:16:20Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <username>MaxSem</username>
        <id>590476</id>
      </contributor>
      <minor />
      <comment>+ru:</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">In [[Greek mythology]], '''Iphicles''' referred to three different people:

#The half-brother of [[Heracles]], being the son of [[Alcmene]] and her human husband  [[Amphitryon]] whereas Heracles was her son by [[Zeus]]. Iphicles was the father of Heracles' charioteer [[Iolaus]].
#Son of [[Thestius]], one of the [[Argonauts]], and a participant in the hunt for the [[Calydonian Boar]], where he was killed by [[Meleager]].
#A [[Thessaly|Thessalonian]] man, son of [[Phylacus]], he fathered [[Protesilaus]] and [[Podarces]].

[[Category:Greek mythological people]]

[[bg:Ификъл]]
[[de:Iphikles]]
[[fr:Iphiclès]]
[[lt:Ifiklas]]
[[nl:Iphikles]]
[[ru:Ификл]]</text>
