  <page>
    <title>Santa Anna</title>
    <id>81073</id>
    <revision>
      <id>39420295</id>
      <timestamp>2006-02-13T00:53:23Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <username>Bic1313</username>
        <id>763782</id>
      </contributor>
      <minor />
      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Santa Anna''' is a name referring to different meanings:

*In [[Spanish language|Spanish]] (where it is equivalent to [[Santa Ana]]) and in [[Italian language]], &quot;Santa Anna&quot; is the name of [[Saint Anne]], the mother of the [[Mary, the mother of Jesus|Virgin Mary]].

*[[Antonio López de Santa Anna]] (1794-1876), a [[Mexico|Mexican]] [[soldier]], [[dictator]], [[general]] and statesman who took part in the [[Texas Revolution]] as well as governed Mexico intermittently during the early to mid 1800's.

*'''Santa Anna''' is the name of various cities, including:
**[[Santa Anna, Texas]], [[United States|USA]]

==See also==
* [[Santa Ana]]

{{disambig}}</text>
    </revision>
