  <page>
    <title>Scottish Aviation</title>
    <id>81082</id>
    <revision>
      <id>40625868</id>
      <timestamp>2006-02-21T22:38:27Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <username>TPO-bot</username>
        <id>725128</id>
      </contributor>
      <minor />
      <comment>Robot: Changing template: industry-corp-stub</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">[[image:scottish.twin.750pix.jpg|thumb|200px|Scottish Aviation Twin Pioneer, England, 2003.]]
'''Scottish Aviation''' was a [[Scotland|Scottish]] [[aircraft]] manufacturer, based at [[Prestwick]] in [[South Ayrshire]]. It built robust military [[STOL]] utility aircraft such as the Pioneer and larger [[Twin Pioneer]]. Much later the company built some Jetstream [[turboprop]] transport and navigational training aircraft following the collapse of the [[Handley Page Aircraft Company]] (which designed the type). It built [[Scottish Aviation Bulldog|Bulldog]] trainers after the demise of their original manufacturer, [[Beagle Aircraft Company]], which Scottish Aviation absorbed in [[1970]].  The company merged into [[British Aerospace]] in [[1977]].

{{airlistbox}}

[[Category:Defunct British aircraft manufacturers]]
[[Category:Companies of Scotland]]
[[Category:South Ayrshire]]
[[Category:Aviation in Scotland]]

{{Scotland-stub}}
{{industry-company-stub}}</text>
