      <text xml:space="preserve">The [[Virginia|Commonwealth of Virginia]] is divided into 95 counties and 39 [[independent city|independent cities]], which are considered [[county-equivalent]]s for census puposes.  Note that the map in this article, taken from the official [[United States Census Bureau]] site, includes [[Clifton Forge, Virginia|Clifton Forge]] as an independent city. This reflected the political reality at the time of the [[2000]] Census. However, in [[2001]], Clifton Forge relinquished its city charter and reincorporated as a town. In Virginia, municipalities incorporated as ''towns'' are included in counties. For some counties, the [[Bureau of Economic Analysis]] combines any independent cities with the county that once part of that county until 1871 for statistical purposes.
   
[[Image:Virginia counties and independent cities map.gif|right|620px|Virginia counties and independent cities]]   



