      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Oeagrus''' (''Oeager'') in [[Greek mythology]] was a king of [[Thrace]]. He and the muse [[Calliope]] were possibly the parents of [[Orpheus]] and [[Linus]].

He is sometimes called the son of [[Ares]], but other times [[Charops]] is mentioned as his father, which explains his inheritance of the throne.

