    <title>Don</title>
    <id>81257</id>
    <revision>
      <id>42006733</id>
      <timestamp>2006-03-03T04:28:45Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <ip>70.128.83.46</ip>
      </contributor>
      <text xml:space="preserve">The term '''Don''' may refer to:
* [[Don]], [[Donald Duck]]'s nickname.

* ''Don'', the term used for a crime or [[mafia]] leader.

* [[Don, Nord]], a ''[[Commune in France|commune]]'' of the [[Nord (département)|Nord]] ''[[département in France|département]]'' in northern [[France]]

* [[Dôn]], a mother [[goddess]] in [[Welsh mythology]]

* an abbreviated/diminutive form of the Western male name '''Donald'''.

* in English [[university|universities]], traditionally, a head, fellow or tutor of a [[college]] (''see also [[Superdon]]'')

* In pharmacology, DON refers to the psychedelic phenethylamine [[2,5-dimethoxy-4-nitroamphetamine]]

* in [[Spanish language|Spanish]] and [[Italian language|Italian]], Don is a nobility title for a [[male]], prefixed to the name, often paired alone with the first/Christian name (e.g. [[Don Juan]], [[Don Quixote]], [[Don Giovanni]]). It is abbreviated as ''[[D.]]''. The female for Don is Doña (eg. [[Doña Concepcion]]).

* In Sri Lankan culture those of Portuguese decent some people of higher caste were bestowed the title of [[Don]] for men and [[Doña]] for women.e.g. [[Don]] Manoj Gihan Silvapulle 
* An (obsolescent) colloquial term for a [[Spain|Spanish]] person. The word appears in [[Henry Newbolt]]'s poem &quot;[[Drake's Drum]]&quot;: ''&quot;If the dons sight Devon, I'll quit the port of heaven...&quot;''. 

* An [[Ashkenazi]] variant transliteration of [[Tribe of Dan|Dan]], the [[tribes of Israel|tribe of Israel]].

* An acronymn for the United States [[Department_of_the_Navy|Department of the Navy]]

*[[DON Smallgoods]], an Australian smallgoods company with the gutterally pronounced slogan &quot;Iz Don. Iz Good.&quot;

==Rivers==

* [[Don River, Russia]], one of the main rivers of Russia.

* [[River Don, Aberdeenshire|River Don, Scotland]], a river in [[Aberdeenshire (traditional)|Aberdeenshire]] which rises in the [[Grampian Mountains (Scotland)|Grampians]] and flows 131 km (82 miles) eastwards to the [[North Sea]] at [[Aberdeen, Scotland|Aberdeen]].

*[[River Don, England]], a river in [[South Yorkshire]] which rises in the [[Pennines]] and flows 112 km (70 miles) eastwards to join the [[River Ouse, Yorkshire|Yorkshire Ouse]] shortly before it, in turn, flows into the [[Humber]].

*[[Don River (Toronto)]] is one of two major rivers framing [[Toronto]] against [[Lake Ontario]].

==Movie==
* Don (1978) is a blockbuster hindi movie starring [[Amitabh|Amitabh Bacchan]].

==TV Series==
* DON is the name of a TV series aired on [[Star One]]. DON is the nickname and the letters are the initials of the protagonist's name: Detective Omkar Nath.

{{disambig}}

