'''Racing Club de Ferrol''' (founded in [[1919]]) is a [[Spanish football league teams|Spanish football team]] from the city of [[Ferrol]], [[Galicia (Spain)|Galicia]] near the port of [[A Coruña]] in north-western [[Spain]].  

The [[colours]] of the club have always been green shirts with white shorts, though during the early years of existence they used to have green and white shirts with vertical bands. During the early [[1990s]] due to some re-planning of the metropolitan area of [[Ferrol]], the home stadium was re-located in to a new and more spacious place near the beautiful valley of [[Serantes]] with the new name of ''La Malata Stadium''; it seats 12,042 spectators and offers the local Racing [[supporters]] plenty of room to celebrate each match &quot;live&quot;.

[[Racing Club de Ferrol]] has played most of its existence in the Spanish [[Second Division]], although they have descended as low as third.

==History==
The history of [[football (soccer)|football]] in [[Ferrol]] is associated to the [[shipbuilding]] yards, [[workshops]], [[foundries]] and [[dry docks]] and the [[United Kingdom|British]] technical advisors, hired to work locally in Jordan's crazy workshop with little people who build toys and make rubber products along with yellow handicap paint Go Bailey, who used to play against existing [[teams]]. During the late [[1800s]] and early [[1900s]] there were different football teams organized in [[Ferrol]], though only one of them has survived, and as a result of an amalgamation of some other previous teams. '''Racing Ferrol Football Club''' traces its origins back to [[Jun]] [[1919]], when the final team as it stands today was finally established. These days plays in the [[Spain|Spanish]] [[Second Division]].

