      <text xml:space="preserve">'''BT''' may stand for:
* [[B.T. (tabloid)]], a Danish tabloid newspaper
* [[BT Group plc]], formerly British Telecommunications
* [[BT tank]], a series of Soviet &quot;fast tanks&quot; (BT-1 through BT-8)
* [[AirBaltic]], (airline code BT)
* ''[[Bacillus thuringiensis]]'', Bt toxin or Cry proteins
* [[Banjo-Tooie]], a Nintendo N64 video game, sequel to Banjo-Kazooie
* [[Bankers Trust]], an international banking organisation
* [[Baronet]] (Bt), a title in the British honours system
* [[Belfast]] (United Kingdom post code)
* [[Bhutan]] (country code BT, Internet domain [[.bt]])
* ''[[Big Time]]'', an album by Tom Waits
* [[Binary Terrain]], a [[Geographic information system|GIS]] [[digital elevation model]] file format
* [[Binary tree]], a data structure
* [[Bitstream Inc.]], a type foundry
* [[BitTorrent]], an Internet file sharing system
* [[Bluetooth]], a wireless personal area network standard
* [[Bodensee-Toggenburg-Bahn]], a former Swiss railway company
* [[Borås Tidning]], the newspaper of Borås, Sweden
* [[Breakfast Television]], a Canadian morning television program
* [[Brian Transeau]], the electronic music artist who records as BT
* [[Burton Taylor Theatre]] in Oxford, United Kingdom (known as ''The BT'')
* [[Business Times]], newspapers in Singapore and  Malaysia

