      <minor />
      <comment>Reverted edits by [[Special:Contributions/195.92.168.164|195.92.168.164]] ([[User talk:195.92.168.164|talk]]) to last version by Rich Farmbrough</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">[[Image:JoGuestCover.jpg|thumb|right|250px|Jo Guest on the cover of ''[[Club International (magazine)]]''.]]
'''Joanne Guest''' (born [[February 22]], [[1972]] in [[Chesterfield, Derbyshire]]) is a British [[glamour model]] who has become a minor [[celebrity]] in her own right. She has appeared in a wide range of British &amp;quot;top shelf&amp;quot; magazines, including ''[[Mayfair (magazine)|Mayfair]]'' and ''Men Only''. Since [[2000]] she has been a television host for the [[Men and Motors]] cable/satellite channel in the [[United Kingdom]], operated by [[Granada Television|Granada]]. 

Born and raised in [[Chesterfield]], North East [[Derbyshire]], [[England]], Guest got her start in modeling when she came across an advertisement for modeling, while she was attending college. She appeared as a [[Page 3]] girl in ''[[The Sun (newspaper)|The Sun]]'' and has appeared in magazines like ''[[Loaded]]'' and ''[[FHM]]'', among the others previously mentioned. She also appeared in the ''[[Playboy]]'' video ''[[Shagalicious British Babes]]''.

She was one of the first models to successfully appear on both soft core glamour and more explicit magazines. Indeed Jo would often pose showing both her anus and her vulva, and in many pictures the full length of her vaginal slit from behind, a trend of glamour photography which only started in the UK in the 1990's. She became one of the few models able to pose to show her vagina from behind whilst also keeping her breasts in the shot.

Jo did pose for some simulated hardcore shots. There are no known picture showing actual penetration. There is one picture showing her taking a penis into her mouth but her hand in the picture prevents the observer from seeing whether this is for real.

Starting with the [[June]] [[2002]] issue, Guest had a monthly advice column in ''[[Front (magazine)|Front]]'' magazine. This wasn't her first foray into this genre, as she had previously appeared in a weekly &amp;quot;agony babe&amp;quot; advice column in the ''[[Daily Star]]'' newspaper (from [[November]] [[1998]] to [[March]] [[2000]]).

In 2003, she started appearing exclusively every month in the British magazine ''[[Men's World (magazine)|Men's World]]'' with whom she also started an interactive website (details in Joanne Guest Links [http://groups.yahoo.com/group/joanneguestlinks]). But she did not feature in the November or December issues, it being said she was too busy.

==TV career==
Guest has hosted a number of television programmes on the [[Granada Television|Granada]] [[Men &amp; Motors]] cable/satellite channel in the [[United Kingdom]]. Shows include:

* ''Jo Guest's Private Parts'' (Nov 1998)
* ''Undressed with Guest'' (the second series was shown in Spring 1999)
* ''Jo Guest in Jamaica'' (Jan-Feb 2000)
* ''Jo Guest&amp;amp;#8217;s Capital Exposed'' (Nov 2002)
* ''Jo Guest's The Steam Room'' (Oct 2004)
* ''Jo Guest UK Exposed'' (Nov 2004)

==External links==
* {{imdb|id=1181350|name=Jo Guest}}
* [http://www.zedtoo.demon.co.uk/jgfaq/ Jo Guest FAQ] (text only)

