  <page>
    <title>Shelby County, Alabama</title>
    <id>81310</id>
    <revision>
      <id>27296884</id>
      <timestamp>2005-11-03T23:44:59Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <ip>68.221.192.37</ip>
      </contributor>
      <comment>Q</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">&lt;div style=&quot;float:right; margin: 0 0 1em 1em;&quot;&gt;[[Image:Shelby County Alabama.png]]&lt;/div&gt;
'''Shelby County''' is a [[county]] of the [[U.S. state|State]] of [[Alabama]] and is named in honor of [[Isaac Shelby]], [[Governor of Kentucky]].    The [[county seat]] of Shelby County is [[Columbiana, Alabama|Columbiana]].  As of [[2000]] [[U.S. Census]], the population was 143,293.  As of [[2004]] estimates the county has about 165,677.  Shelby County is ranked the fastest growing county in Alabama and one of the fastest growing counties in the country.

== History ==
Shelby County was established on [[February 7]], [[1818]].

== Geography ==
According to the [[United States Census Bureau|U.S. Census Bureau]], the county has a total area of 2,097 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (810 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  2,058 km&amp;sup2; (795 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 38 km&amp;sup2; (15 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is water.  The total area is 1.83% water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]][[Geographic references#2|&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;]] of [[2000]], there are 143,293 people, 54,631 households, and 40,590 families residing in the county.  The [[population density]] is 70/km&amp;sup2; (180/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 59,302 housing units at an average density of 29/km&amp;sup2; (75/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the county is 89.80% [[Race (U.S. census)|White]], 7.40% [[Race (U.S. census)|Black]] or [[Race (U.S. census)|African American]], 0.33% [[Race (U.S. census)|Native American]], 1.03% [[Race (U.S. census)|Asian]], 0.02% [[Race (U.S. census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.71% from [[race (U.S. census)|other races]], and 0.72% from two or more races.  2.03% of the population are [[Race (U.S. census)|Hispanic]] or [[Race (U.S. census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 54,631 households out of which 36.70% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 63.60% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 8.10% have a female householder with no husband present, and 25.70% are non-families. 21.70% of all households are made up of individuals and 5.20% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.59 and the average family size is 3.04.

In the county the population is spread out with 26.30% under the age of 18, 8.20% from 18 to 24, 33.70% from 25 to 44, 23.40% from 45 to 64, and 8.50% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 35 years.  For every 100 females there are 96.20 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 92.60 males.

The median income for a household in the county is $55,440, and the median income for a family is $64,105. Males have a median income of $45,798 versus $31,242 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the county is $27,176.  6.30% of the population and 4.60% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 7.10% of those under the age of 18 and 8.20% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

== Municipalities and census-designated places ==
*[[Alabaster, Alabama|Alabaster]]
*[[Birmingham, Alabama|Birmingham]] (part - part of Birmingham is in [[Jefferson County, Alabama|Jefferson County]])
*[[Calera, Alabama|Calera]] (part - part of Calera is in [[Chilton County, Alabama|Chilton County]])
*[[Chelsea, Alabama|Chelsea]]
*[[Childersburg, Alabama|Childersburg]] (part - part of Childersburg is in [[Talladega County, Alabama|Talladega County]])
*[[Columbiana, Alabama|Columbiana]]
*[[Harpersville, Alabama|Harpersville]]
*[[Helena, Alabama|Helena]] (part - part of Helena is in [[Jefferson County, Alabama|Jefferson County]])
*[[Hoover, Alabama|Hoover]] (part - part of Hoover is in [[Jefferson County, Alabama|Jefferson County]])
*[[Indian Springs Village, Alabama|Indian Springs Village]]
*[[Lake Purdy, Alabama|Lake Purdy]]
*[[Leeds, Alabama|Leeds]] (part - part of Leeds is in [[Jefferson County, Alabama|Jefferson County]] and in [[St. Clair County, Alabama|St. Clair County]])
*[[Meadowbrook, Alabama|Meadowbrook]]
*[[Montevallo, Alabama|Montevallo]]
*[[Pelham, Alabama|Pelham]]
*[[Vestavia Hills, Alabama|Vestavia Hills]] (part - part of Vestavia Hills is in [[Jefferson County, Alabama|Jefferson County]])
*[[Vincent, Alabama|Vincent]] (part - part of Vincent is in [[St. Clair County, Alabama|St. Clair County]] and in [[Talladega County, Alabama|Talladega County]])
*[[Westover, Alabama|Westover]]
*[[Wilsonville, Alabama|Wilsonville]]
*[[Wilton, Alabama|Wilton]]

== External links ==
* [http://www.shelbycountyalabama.com/ Shelby County Government]
* [http://www.shelbycounty.com Shelby County Web Portal]

