      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Shelby County''' is a [[county]] located in the [[U.S. state|state]] of [[Iowa]].  As of [[2000]], the population is 13,173. Its name is in honor of [[Isaac Shelby]], [[Governor of Kentucky]].  Its [[county seat]] is [[Harlan, Iowa]][[Geographic references|&lt;sup&gt;6&lt;/sup&gt;]].
&lt;div style=&quot;float:right;width:300px;margin-left:5px&quot;&gt;[[Image:Map of Iowa highlighting Shelby County.png]]&lt;/div&gt;

== Geography ==
According to the [[United States Census Bureau|U.S. Census Bureau]], the county has a total area of 1,532 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (591 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  1,530 km&amp;sup2; (591 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 1 km&amp;sup2; (1 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is water.  The total area is 0.09% water.

=== Adjacent counties ===
