*[[Audubon County, Iowa|Audubon County]]  (east)
*[[Cass County, Iowa|Cass County]]  (southeast)
*[[Pottawattamie County, Iowa|Pottawattamie County]]  (south)
*[[Harrison County, Iowa|Harrison County]]  (west)

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]][[Geographic references#2|&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;]] of [[2000]], there are 13,173 people, 5,173 households, and 3,703 families residing in the county.  The [[population density]] is 9/km&amp;sup2; (22/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 5,459 housing units at an average density of 4/km&amp;sup2; (9/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the county is 98.68% [[Race (U.S. census)|White]], 0.10% [[Race (U.S. census)|Black]] or [[Race (U.S. census)|African American]], 0.29% [[Race (U.S. census)|Native American]], 0.27% [[Race (U.S. census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Race (U.S. census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.18% from [[race (U.S. census)|other races]], and 0.48% from two or more races.  0.67% of the population are [[Race (U.S. census)|Hispanic]] or [[Race (U.S. census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 5,173 households out of which 32.60% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 62.30% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 6.80% have a female householder with no husband present, and 28.40% are non-families. 25.20% of all households are made up of individuals and 13.60% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.49 and the average family size is 2.99.

In the county the population is spread out with 26.40% under the age of 18, 5.70% from 18 to 24, 25.20% from 25 to 44, 22.40% from 45 to 64, and 20.40% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 40 years.  For every 100 females there are 95.90 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 93.30 males.

The median income for a household in the county is $37,442, and the median income for a family is $44,681. Males have a median income of $29,402 versus $20,296 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the county is $16,969.  6.00% of the population and 4.30% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 6.00% of those under the age of 18 and 7.60% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

