      <text xml:space="preserve">&lt;div style=&quot;float:right; margin: 0 0 1em 1em;&quot;&gt;[[Image:Wilcox County Alabama.png]]&lt;/div&gt;
'''Wilcox County''' is a [[county]] of the [[U.S. state]] of [[Alabama]]. Its name is in honor of Lieutenant J. M. Wilcox, who fought in the wars against the [[Creek (people)|Creek]] [[Native American (U.S.)|Indians]].  As of [[2000]] the population was 13,183.  Its [[county seat]] is [[Camden, Alabama|Camden]].

== History ==
Wilcox County was established on [[December 13]], [[1819]].

== Geography ==
According to the [[United States Census Bureau|U.S. Census Bureau]], the county has a total area of 2,350 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (907 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  2,302 km&amp;sup2; (889 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 49 km&amp;sup2; (19 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is water.  The total area is 2.07% water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]][[Geographic references#2|&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;]] of [[2000]], there are 13,183 people, 4,776 households, and 3,376 families residing in the county.  The [[population density]] is 6/km&amp;sup2; (15/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 6,183 housing units at an average density of 3/km&amp;sup2; (7/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the county is 27.51% [[Race (U.S. census)|White]], 71.90% [[Race (U.S. census)|Black]] or [[Race (U.S. census)|African American]], 0.14% [[Race (U.S. census)|Native American]], 0.13% [[Race (U.S. census)|Asian]], 0.02% [[Race (U.S. census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.11% from [[race (U.S. census)|other races]], and 0.19% from two or more races.  0.74% of the population are [[Race (U.S. census)|Hispanic]] or [[Race (U.S. census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 4,776 households out of which 36.00% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 39.80% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 26.50% have a female householder with no husband present, and 29.30% are non-families. 27.50% of all households are made up of individuals and 11.90% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.70 and the average family size is 3.31.

In the county the population is spread out with 30.70% under the age of 18, 9.10% from 18 to 24, 25.50% from 25 to 44, 21.00% from 45 to 64, and 13.70% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 34 years.  For every 100 females there are 87.20 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 81.00 males.

The median income for a household in the county is $16,646, and the median income for a family is $22,200. Males have a median income of $26,216 versus $17,274 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the county is $10,903.  39.90% of the population and 36.10% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 48.40% of those under the age of 18 and 32.10% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

== Cities and towns ==
*[[Camden, Alabama|Camden]]
*[[Oak Hill, Alabama|Oak Hill]]
*[[Pine Apple, Alabama|Pine Apple]]
*[[Pine Hill, Alabama|Pine Hill]]
*[[Yellow Bluff, Alabama|Yellow Bluff]]

{{Alabama}}

[[Category:Alabama counties]]

[[Category:Wilcox County, Alabama| ]]</text>
