      <contributor>
        <username>FlaBot</username>
        <id>228773</id>
      </contributor>
      <minor />
      <comment>robot  Adding: pl</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">&lt;div class=&quot;messagebox cleanup metadata&quot;&gt;'''To meet Wikipedia's [[:Category:Wikipedia style guidelines|quality standards]], this article or section may require [[Wikipedia:Cleanup|cleanup]].''' &lt;br /&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 90%&quot;&gt;
See rationale on the [[Talk:{{PAGENAME}}|talk page]], or replace this tag with a [[Wikipedia:Template_messages/Cleanup#Cleanup_.E2.80.94_specific_issues|more specific message]]. [[Help:Editing|Editing help]] is available.&lt;br /&gt;(Tagged February 2006)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;[[Category:Cleanup from February 2006]]
Originally, '''Kahuna''' was the [[Hawaii]]an title for a priest, expert, teacher, and/or adviser, and the term is still used in that context by native Hawaiians.  (See [[ancient Hawaii|ancient Hawai'i]])  A ''kahuna nui'' was a high priest.  

In [[beach movies]] of the [[1960s]] (et seq.) such as ''[[Beach Blanket Bingo]]'', the &quot;Big Kahuna&quot; was the best surfer on the beach. This term later made its way from Hollywood into general [[surfing]] culture.  (See also &quot;[[Duke Kahanamoku|The Big Kahuna]]&quot;.) 

In some computer programming shops (for example, [[International Business Machines|IBM]]), &quot;kahuna&quot; is a synonym for &quot;wizard&quot; or &quot;guru&quot; (see [[internet slang]]).

[http://channel9.msdn.com/showpost.aspx?postid=118322 Kahuna] is also the name of mail software in development at [[Microsoft]].

[[Category:Surf culture]]
[[Category:Religion in Hawaii]]

[[pl:Kahuna]]</text>
