      </contributor>
      <comment>ecuador</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Santa Ana''' is the [[Spanish language|Spanish-language]] name of [[Saint Anne]], the mother of [[Mary, the mother of Jesus]].

There are a number of places and things named directly or indirectly for her:
*[[Argentina]]
**[[Santa Ana, Misiones]]
*[[Costa Rica]]
**[[Santa Ana, Costa Rica]]
**[[Santa Ana, Canton]]
*[[Ecuador]]
**[[Santa Ana, Ecuador]]
**[[Santa Ana Canton]] ([[Manabí Province]])
*[[El Salvador]]
**[[Santa Ana, El Salvador]]
**[[Santa Ana Volcano]]
*[[Mexico]]
**[[Santa Ana, Oaxaca]]
**[[Santa Ana, Sonora]]
*[[Philippines]]
**[[Santa Ana, Cagayan]]
**[[Santa Ana, Pampanga]]
*[[United States]]
**[[Santa Ana, California]]
**[[Santa Ana Pueblo]], a [[Native Americans in the United States|Native American]] tribe in [[New Mexico]]
**[[Santa Ana River]] in [[California]]
**[[Santa Ana wind]], felt in [[California]]
*[[Venezuela]]
**[[Santa Ana, Anzoátegui]]

'''Santa Ana''' is also a variant spelling of the name of [[Antonio López de Santa Anna]] (1794-1876), a [[Mexico|Mexican]] [[general]] and [[president]] who governed [[Mexico]] intermittently during the first half of the 19th century and who took part in the [[Texas Revolution]]. 

==See also== 
*[[Santa Anna]]
*[[Carlos Santana|Santana]]
*[[Antonio López de Santa Anna]]

{{disambig}}

[[de:Santa Ana]]
[[es:Santa Ana]]
[[pt:Santa Ana (desambiguação)]]</text>
