      <contributor>
        <username>Antonio Basto</username>
        <id>344593</id>
      </contributor>
      <comment>/* Emperors of Brazil (1822&amp;ndash;1889) */</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">The '''Brazilian monarchs''' were the rulers of [[Brazil]] from its discovery in 1500 until 1889. There are three main stages in the dynastical history of Brazil: Brazil as part of the Kingdom of Portugal (1500&amp;ndash;1815), the Kingdom of Brazil (1815&amp;ndash;1822) united with Portugal, and the independent Empire of Brazil (1822&amp;ndash;1889).

Brazil was officially discovered on [[April 22]], [[1500]] and based on the [[Treaty of Tordesilhas]], it became a possession of [[Portugal]]. The Kings of Portugal then were the Monarchs ''in'' Brazil until [[Napoleon]]'s invading army forced the Portuguese government to flee to Brazil in 1807. On [[December 16]], [[1815]] the regent [[John VI of Portugal|D. João VI]] raised Brazil to the status of a kingdom and thus making his mother, the reigning Queen, the first Monarch ''of'' Brazil. Having proclaimed independence from Portugal in [[1822]], [[Pedro I of Brazil|Pedro I]], son of João VI, was crowned Emperor of Brazil on [[December 1]], [[1822]].

== Monarchs in Brazil (1500&amp;ndash;1815) ==

: '''House of Aviz'''
* [[Manuel I of Portugal|D. Manuel I]] ([[1500]]&amp;ndash;[[1521]])
* [[John III of Portugal|D. João III]] ([[1521]]&amp;ndash;[[1557]])
* [[Sebastian I of Portugal|D. Sebastiao I]] ([[1557]]&amp;ndash;[[1578]]) 
* [[Cardinal Henry of Portugal|Cardinal D. Henrique]] ([[1578]]&amp;ndash;[[1580]]) 

: '''House of Habsburg'''
* [[Philip II of Spain|Philip I]] ([[1580]]&amp;ndash;[[1598]])
* [[Philip III of Spain|Philip II]] ([[1598]]&amp;ndash;[[1621]])
* [[Philip IV of Spain|Philip III]] ([[1621]]&amp;ndash;[[1640]])

: '''House of Braganza'''
* [[John IV of Portugal|D. João IV]] ([[1640]]&amp;ndash;[[1656]])
* [[Alphonso VI of Portugal|D. Afonso VI]] ([[1656]]&amp;ndash;[[1667]]) 
* [[Peter II of Portugal|D. Pedro II]] ([[1667]]&amp;ndash;[[1706]])
* [[John V of Portugal|D. João V]] ([[1706]]&amp;ndash;[[1750]])
* [[Joseph Emanuel of Portugal|D. José Emanuel]] ([[1750]]&amp;ndash;[[1777]])
* [[Peter III of Portugal|D. Pedro III]] ([[1777]]&amp;ndash;[[1786]])

== Monarchs of Brazil (1815&amp;ndash;1822)==
* [[Maria I of Portugal|D. Maria I]] ([[1777]]&amp;ndash;[[1816]])
* [[John VI of Portugal|D. João VI]] (Regency 1792&amp;ndash;1816, Reign [[1816]]&amp;ndash;[[1822]])

== Emperors of Brazil (1822&amp;ndash;1889) == 
* [[Pedro I of Brazil|Pedro I]] ([[1822]]&amp;ndash;[[1831]])
* [[Pedro II of Brazil|Pedro II]] ([[1831]]&amp;ndash;[[1889]])
** Regência Provisória (Regency 1831)
** Regência Permanente (Regency 1831&amp;ndash;1835)
** [[Diogo Antônio Feijó]] (Regency 1835&amp;ndash;1837)
** [[Pedro de Araújo Lima]] (Regency 1837&amp;ndash;1840)
** Isabel (Imperial Princess Regent 1871&amp;ndash;1872, 1876&amp;ndash;1877, 1887&amp;ndash;1888).

== Pretenders of Brazilian monarchy (1889&amp;ndash;present) ==

See [[List of heads of the Brazilian Imperial House]]

