    <title>Jumping Jack</title>
    <id>81462</id>
    <revision>
      <id>37286294</id>
      <timestamp>2006-01-30T00:46:21Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <username>Alexrudd</username>
        <id>156530</id>
      </contributor>
      <minor />
      <comment>Disambiguation link repair</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">A '''Jumping Jack''' is a physical [[exercise]] performed by [[jump|jumping]] to a position with the [[Human_leg|legs]] spread wide and the [[hand|hands]] touching overhead and then returning to a position with the [[foot|feet]] together and the [[arm|arms]] at the sides.  The term can also refer to a [[toy]] figure with jointed limbs that can be made to [[dance]] by pulling an attached string.

More intensive versions include bending down and touching the floor in between each jump.

It is also commonly known as &quot;star jumps&quot;, especially to children of commonwealth nations.

== See also ==
* [[Jack McFadden]], also known as '''Jack &quot;Jumping Jack&quot; McFadden''', named greatest player of all time by the [[Amateur Athletic Union|AAU]].
* [[Jumping Jack (game)]] a computer game by [[Imagine Software|Imagine]] of Liverpool.

[[Category:Aerobic exercise]]</text>
    </revision>
