  <page>
    <title>Marianne Fredriksson</title>
    <id>81516</id>
    <revision>
      <id>37561257</id>
      <timestamp>2006-01-31T20:06:35Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <username>Frecklefoot</username>
        <id>4259</id>
      </contributor>
      <comment>+sub-sections, titles need itals</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Marianne Fredriksson''' (born [[Gothenburg]], [[March 28]], [[1927]]) is a [[Sweden|Swedish]] [[author]]. Before becoming a novelist, she was a [[journalist]] on various Swedish [[newspaper]]s and [[magazine]]s, including [[Svenska Dagbladet]].

So far, she has published eleven novels, all of which have been translated into [[English language|English]], [[German language|German]] and other languages. The central theme in her writings is friendship because, according to Marianne herself, &quot;friendship will be more important than love&quot; in the future.

==Bibliography==
===Fiction===
*Nightwanderer (&quot;Den Som Vandrar om Natten&quot;, 2003)
*Loved children (''Älskade barn'', 2001)
*Children of Paradise (&quot;Paradisets Barn&quot;, 2000)
*[[According to Mary Magdalene]] (''Enligt Maria Magdalena'', 1999)
*Inge &amp; Mira (&quot;Flyttfåglar&quot;, 1999)
*Hanna's Daughters (''Anna, Hanna och Johanna'', 1994)
*Sofie (&quot;Blindgång&quot;, 1994)
*Simon and the Oaks (''Simon och ekarna'', 1991)
*The Enigma (''Gåtan'', 1990)
*The Saga of Norea (&quot;Noreas Saga&quot;, 1986)
*The Book of [[Cain]] (''Kains bok'', 1981)
*The Book of [[Eve]] (''Evas bok'', 1980) 

===Non-fiction===
*The Conditions of the Acacia (&quot;På Akacians Villkor&quot;), written together with architect Bengt Warne
*The Eleventh Conspiracy (&quot;De Elva Sammansvurna&quot;), 1997, written together with daughter Ann Fredriksson
*If Women Were Wise the World Would Stop (&quot;Om Kvinnor Vore Kloka Skulle Världen Stanna&quot;, 1995)

[[Category:1927 births|Fredriksson, Marianne]]
[[Category:Living people|Fredriksson, Marianne]]
[[Category:Swedish language writers|Fredriksson, Marianne]]

[[de:Marianne Fredriksson]]
[[sv:Marianne Fredriksson]]</text>
    </revision>
  </page>
