        <id>296804</id>
      </contributor>
      <text xml:space="preserve">In [[Greek mythology]], '''Perieres''' or '''Perieris''', was a son of [[Aeolus]] and husband of [[Gorgophone]].  He was the father of [[Leucippus_(mythology)|Leucippus]] and [[Aphareus]]. 

He is often confused with Gorgophone's second husband, [[Oebalus]] (who was, in some stories, Perieres' son).  With Oebalus, Gorgophone was the mother of [[Tyndareus]], [[Hippocoon]] and [[Icarius]].



[[Category:Greek mythological people]]{{Greek-myth-stub}}</text>
