* [http://www.pinhole.cz/en/pinholedesigner/ Software to aid you in your calculations]
* [http://home.online.no/~gjon/pinhole.htm Pinhole Photography, Jon Grepstad]
* [http://www.pinhole.cz/en/pinholecameras/dirkon_01.html Instructions for making a realistic looking pinhole camera out of cardboard that works with 35mm film]
* [http://www.exploratorium.edu/light_walk/camera_todo.html A simple pinhole camera that works with rare type 126 cartridge film]
* [http://www.pinhole.org/ The Pinhole Gallery]
* [http://www.jeffkorte.com/ Pinhole Camera Photographs by Jeff Korte]
* [http://www.pinholeday.org Worldwide Pinhole Photography Day]
* [http://www.pinholeresource.com PinholeResource.com]
* [http://www.kodak.com/global/en/consumer/education/lessonPlans/pinholeCamera/ Kodak on Pinhole Camera construction]
* [http://www.photo.net/pinhole/pinhole ''Pinhole Photography - History, Images, Cameras, Formulas''] article at [http://www.photo.net Photo.net]
* [http://www.pinholephotography.org Information on making pinhole cameras by Justin Quinnell]
* [http://www.merrillphoto.com/pintoidhowto.htm Marcy's Pintoid how-to page!]
