      </contributor>
      <comment>{{organic-compound-stub}}</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Lipoamide''' is a [[trivial name]] for 6,8-dithiooctanoic amide. It is [[lipoic acid|6,8-dithiooctanoic acid]]'s functional form where the [[carboxyl]] group is attached to [[protein]] (or any other [[amine]]) by an [[amide linkage]] (containing -NH&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;) to a [[amino acid|amino group]].


