  <page>
    <title>List of counties in Georgia</title>
    <id>81618</id>
    <revision>
      <id>28329755</id>
      <timestamp>2005-11-14T20:25:08Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <username>YurikBot</username>
        <id>271058</id>
      </contributor>
      <minor />
      <comment>robot  Modifying: de</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">[[Image:Georgia (U.S. state) counties map.png|right|550px|Georgia (U.S. state) counties]]
'''[[Georgia (U.S. state)|Georgia]]''' has the second-highest number of [[counties]] of any state in the [[United States]], behind [[List of Texas counties|Texas]] (254).  The proliferation of counties in the state led to multiple state [[constitutional amendment]]s, attempting to establish limits.  The most recent such amendment, dating to [[1945]], limits the state to 159 counties, though there were previously 161 from [[1924]] to [[1931]].  In a rare [[consolidation]], [[Campbell County, Georgia|Campbell County]] and [[Milton County, Georgia|Milton County]] were made part of Fulton County as of [[1932]], as an [[austerity]] measure during the [[Great Depression]].

