  <page>
    <title>Orthrus</title>
    <id>81621</id>
    <revision>
      <id>41438676</id>
      <timestamp>2006-02-27T08:48:58Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <username>Ian Pitchford</username>
        <id>230605</id>
      </contributor>
      <comment>[[WP:AWB|AWB assisted]] clean up</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">In [[Greek mythology]], '''Orthrus''' (also called '''Orthros''', '''Orthos''', '''Orthus''', '''Orth''' and '''Orphus''') was a [[multi-headed animal|two-headed]] [[dog]] and the brother of [[Cerberus]].  He was owned by the three-bodied titan, [[Geryon]]. Orthrus and his master, [[Eurytion]], were charged with guarding Geryon's herd of red cattle. [[Heracles]] eventually killed Orthrus, Eurytion, and Geryon, before taking the red cattle to complete his tenth labor.

Orthrus was the son of [[Echidna (mythology)|Echidne]] and [[Typhon]]. His siblings included [[Chimera (creature)|Chimera]], [[Cerberus]], the [[Lernaean Hydra]], [[Ethon]], [[Ladon (mythology)|Ladon]], and sometimes the [[Sphinx]] and [[Nemean Lion]]. Because of the varying genealogies, he may be the father of the Sphinx and the Nemean Lion with either Echidne or Chimera. Due to his mother's relation to Heracles (taken from Herodotus), his half-siblings include [[Agathyrsi]], [[Gelonus]], and [[Scytha]].

[[Category:Greek mythology]]
[[Category:Legendary creatures]]
[[Category:Mythological dogs]]

[[de:Orthos]]
[[es:Ortro]]
[[fr:Orthos]]
[[ja:オルトロス]]
[[lt:Ortas]]
[[pl:Ortros]]


{{greek-myth-stub}}</text>
    </revision>
