      </contributor>
      <minor />
      <comment>lt:</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">In [[Greek mythology]], '''Glauce''' refers to two different people:

#Daughter of [[Creon]], Glauce married [[Jason]].  She was killed, along with Jason's children, by his wife, [[Medea]]. Also known by the name [[Creusa]], predominantly in Latin authors, e.g. Seneca (''Medea'') and Propertius (2.16.30).
#Glauce was one of the [[Nereids]]
{{Greek-myth-stub}} [[category:Greek mythological people]]

[[lt:Glaukė]]</text>
    </revision>
