        <ip>80.25.133.53</ip>
      </contributor>
      <comment>+ast +es</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">In [[Greek mythology]], '''Ourea''' was a rarely mentioned [[god]] of the mountains, son of [[Gaia (mythology)|Gaia]].

The Greek personifications of mountains. Each mountain was said to have its own god. They are of the Protogenoi: the first-born elemental gods, children of [[Gaia (mythology)|Gaia]]. Theogony (129-131), Argonautica (1.498). 

[[Category:Greek gods]]
{{greek-myth-stub}}

