  <page>
    <title>Haemus</title>
    <id>81695</id>
    <revision>
      <id>40730767</id>
      <timestamp>2006-02-22T17:04:57Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <ip>131.111.8.99</ip>
      </contributor>
      <text xml:space="preserve">In [[Greek mythology]], King '''Haemus''' (or '''Haimos''') of [[Thrace]] was the son of [[Boreas]].  He was vain and haughty and compared himself and his wife, [[Rhodope]], to [[Zeus]] and [[Hera]].  They changed him and his wife into mountains ([[Haemus Mons]] and [[Rhodope Mountains]], respectively). In Greek, the Balkan Peninsula was thus known as the Peninsula of Haemus (Χερσόνησος του Αίμου). This naming of the Balkans has some basis amongst todays greeks as well.

[[Category:Greek mythological people]]
[[Category: Thracian kings]]</text>
    </revision>
  </page>
