      <text xml:space="preserve">In [[Greek mythology]], '''Lycomedes''' (also known as [[Lycurgus]]) was the King of [[Skyros]] during the [[Trojan War]].  [[Achilles]] hid himself in Lycomedes' court to escape the war and father [[Neoptolemus]] with Lycomedes' daughter, [[Deidamea]].

[[Plutarch]] says that Lycomedes also killed [[Theseus]] by pushing him off a cliff.

{{Greek-myth-stub}}

