      <text xml:space="preserve">:''For other uses of &quot;Deidamea&quot; or &quot;Deidamia&quot;, see [[Deidamia]].
In [[Greek mythology]], '''Deidamea''', or ''Deidamia'', was the daughter of [[Lycomedes]], King of [[Scyros]].  During the [[Trojan War]], [[Achilles]] hid in her father's court, disguised as a girl.  During this time, she gave birth to Achilles' only son, [[Neoptolemus]].

