  <page>
    <title>Astyanax</title>
    <id>81738</id>
    <revision>
      <id>30113560</id>
      <timestamp>2005-12-04T14:29:40Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <ip>222.121.95.174</ip>
      </contributor>
      <text xml:space="preserve">:''This article is about the mythological character; for the [[fish]] [[genus]], see [[Astyanax (fish)]].''

In [[Greek mythology]], '''Astyanax''' ([[Greek language|Greek]] for ''prince of the city'') was the son of [[Hector]] and [[Andromache]].  His real name was [[Scamandrius]], but people of Troy nicknamed him Astyanax, because he was the son of Hector.  He was killed during the [[Trojan War]] by [[Neoptolemus]], who threw the infant from a wall and told his mother &quot;Since my father ([[Achilles]]) killed his father (Hector) he might try to avenge the death. He also could become King of Troy, and we want no more kings of Troy!&quot;  (''[[Iliad]]'' VI, 403, 466; ''[[Aeneid]]'' II, 457)

Astyanax is also the name of a video game which was released in North America under license by [[Jaleco]] in 1988 for the [[NES]] platform.  It is a side-scrolling adventure game which features ancient Greek battle themes.    

Source: Encyclopedia Mythica, http://www.pantheon.org/articles/a/astyanax.html

[[Category:Greek mythological people]]

