      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Deidamia''' may refer to:
* Deidamia or [[Deidamea]], from Greek mythology.
* [[Deidamia (queen)]], wife of [[Demetrius I of Macedon|Demetrius Poliorcetes]]
* [[Deidamia of Epirus]], last ruler of the Aeacid dynasty.
* [[Deidamia (opera)]], by George Frideric Handel.
* ''[[Deidamia (flower)]], a genus of plants related to the passion flower.
* ''Deidamia'', a former genus of crustaceans, now included in ''[[Polychelidae|Willemoesia]]''.

