      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Memnon''' may refer to three men:

*[[Memnon (mythology)]], in Greek mythology

*[[Memnon of Heraclea]] was a Greek historian. In about the [[1st century]] he wrote a history of [[Heraclea Pontica]], a city in [[Asia Minor]] on the [[Black Sea]]. Considerable extracts of Memnon's work are preserved by [[Photius]], arguably the most significant specimen of the Greek local history;

*[[Memnon of Rhodes]] ([[380 BC|380]]&amp;ndash;[[333 BC]]): was the commander of the Greek mercenaries working for the Persian King [[Darius III]] when [[Alexander the Great]] of [[Macedon|Macedonia]] invaded Persia in [[334 BC]] and won the [[Battle of the Granicus River]].

{{disambig}}

[[Category:Ancient Greeks]]
[[Category:People who fought in the Trojan War]]

