      <minor />
      <text xml:space="preserve">The word may have one of the following meanings.

*In [[Greek mythology]], '''Nestor''' was the son of [[Neleus]], the King of [[Pylos]] and [[Chloris]].  See [[Nestor (mythology)]].

*[[Nestor, Greece|Nestor]] is also an archaeological site and a municipality in the west-southwestern part of [[Messenia]]

*[[Nestor the Chronicler]] is a compiler of the [[Primary Chronicle]] of the East [[Slavic peoples|Slavic]] peoples.

*The [[Institute of Astroparticle Physics Nestor]] in the town of [[Pylos]] in [[Greece]] operates a deep sea [[Neutrino]] telescope in the [[Ionian Sea]]

*In [[Ornithology]], '''[[Nestor (genus)|Nestor]]''' is a [[genus]] of [[parrot]]s.

*'''[[Nestor (Tintin character)|Nestor]]''' is a [[fictional]] character from [[Belgium|Belgian]] [[artist]] [[Hergé]]'s renowned [[Tintin]] [[comics|comic]] strip books.

*In the [[Star Trek]] universe, a '''Nestor''' is a legal advisor to the offender in [[Cardassian]] criminal trials.  Unlike the defense lawyer, the Nestor is barred from directly addressing the tribunal.

*In the book ''[[I, Robot]]'' and the movie ''[[I, Robot (movie)|I, Robot]]'', '''Nestor''' is the common nickname of NS-series robots.

*'''[[Ulysses (novel)#Nestor|Nestor]]''' is a chapter in [[James Joyce|James Joyce's]] novel [[Ulysses (novel)|Ulysses]].

*[[Nestor Burma]] is a fictional detective created by the French author [[Léo Malet]].

{{disambig}}

