      <text xml:space="preserve">In [[Greek mythology]], '''Arcesius''', or '''Arkêsios''', also spelled Arceisius, was the son of [[Cephalus]], and King of [[Ithaca]].  He was father of [[Laertes]], and thus grandfather of [[Odysseus]].  Laertes's wife, and thus mother of Laertes, was Chalcomedusa, whose origins are not mentioned further.

''[[Odyssey]]'' XIV, 182.
