      <comment>added to Category:Objectivists</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Terry Goodkind'''  is an [[United States|American]] writer, author of the [[Sword of Truth]] series of [[fantasy]] novels.

== Published Writings ==

[[Image:TerryGoodkind.jpg|Terry Goodkind|right]]

Currently the following books have been released:

* ''[[Wizard's First Rule]]'' (1994)
* ''[[Stone of Tears]]'' (1995)
* ''[[Blood of the Fold]]'' (1996)
* ''[[Temple of the Winds]]'' (1997)
* ''[[Soul of the Fire]]'' (1999)
* ''[[Faith of the Fallen]]'' (2000)
* ''[[The Pillars of Creation]]'' (2001)
* ''[[Naked Empire]]'' (2003)
* The [[Chainfire Trilogy]]:
** ''[[Chainfire]]'' (2005)
** ''[[Phantom (Sword of Truth)|Phantom]]'' (to be released June 2006)

The 2001 ''Legends'' anthology, edited by [[Robert Silverberg]], features a short story, ''[[Debt of Bones]]'', set a few decades before the events in the main series. Later the same year, it was published as a stand-alone [[novella]].

== Life and Success ==

Terry Goodkind has been called one of the most phenomenally successful of all the new fantasy writers of the 1990s, an international bestseller.  According to his Web site, [http://www.terrygoodkind.com www.terrygoodkind.com], he is driven to excel in whatever he turns his attention to doing.  Goodkind was born (in [[1948]]) and raised in [[Omaha, Nebraska|Omaha]], [[Nebraska]], where he also attended schooling in art and Catholic Catechism Instruction.  

Suffering from [[dyslexia]], which in high school brought him &quot;constant ridicule and humiliation from his teachers,&quot; he dropped out of college and worked as a carpenter, a violin maker, a marine and wildlife artist, and a restorer of rare and exotic artifacts and antiques, before turning his thoughts to writing while constructing his home on the forested [[Mount Desert Island]] off the coast of [[Maine]] in [[1983]] with his wife, Jeri.  After years of planning, he began to write his first novel, [[Wizard's First Rule]], in [[1993]], and his writing career was launched with its publication in [[1994]].  In addition to his home in Maine, Goodkind currently lives in the western United States.

Terry Goodkind has been largely influenced by the books of [[Ayn Rand]] and is a strong supporter of her works and of the [[Objectivist philosophy|Objectivist]] Movement.  Many claim that his interpretations and beliefs in her works increasingly pervade the narrative and themes of later books in the series, however he denies this (he claims they were there from the beginning).

== Awards ==
1995 - British Fantasy Award, Icarus (Newcomer) (Nomination)

1995 - Wizard's First Rule [[Locus Award|Locus Poll Award]], Best First Novel (Place: 7)
 
1996 - Stone of Tears [[Locus Award|Locus Poll Award]], Best Fantasy Novel (Place: 15)

1996 - Stone of Tears SFBC Award, The Science Fiction Book Club's Book of the Year Award (Nomination)

1997 - Blood of the Fold [[Locus Award|Locus Poll Award]], Best Fantasy Novel (Place: 18)

1999 - [[Locus Award|Locus Poll Award]], Best SF/Fantasy Author of the 90's (Place: 49)

2004 - [[Prometheus Award]] - Naked Empire (Place: 4)

==External links==
* [http://www.terrygoodkind.com  The Official Terry Goodkind website]
* [http://www.terrygoodkind.net  A site endorsed by Terry Goodkind] Here you can find various topic of discussions about the Sword of Truth Series, current comments from Terry Goodkind himself, as well as up to the moment information.
* {{isfdb name|id=Terry_Goodkind|name=Terry Goodkind}}

{{swordoftruth}}

