  <page>
    <title>Loire Valley</title>
    <id>81870</id>
    <revision>
      <id>38015325</id>
      <timestamp>2006-02-03T16:43:43Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <username>David Justin</username>
        <id>379790</id>
      </contributor>
      <comment>Added link</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Loire Valley''' ([[French language|French]]: ''Vallée de la Loire'') is known as the ''Garden of France'' and the ''Cradle of the French Language''.  It is also noteworthy for the quality of its architectural heritage, in its historic towns such as [[Amboise]], [[Blois]], [[Chinon]], [[Orléans]], [[Saumur]], and [[Tours]], but in particular for its world-famous castles, such as the Châteaux [[Chateau Amboise|Amboise]], [[Chateau Chambord|Chambord]] and [[Château de Chenonceau|Chenonceau]].

The landscape of the Loire Valley, and more particularly its many cultural monuments, illustrate to an exceptional degree the ideals of the [[Renaissance]] and the [[The Enlightenment|Age of the Enlightenment]] on western European thought and design. The Loire Valley is an outstanding cultural landscape of great beauty, containing historic towns and villages, great architectural monuments, its many [[château]]x, and fine [[wine]]s.

On [[December 2]], [[2000]], [[UNESCO]] named the central part of the [[Loire River]] valley, between [[Maine_River|Maine]] and [[Sully-sur-Loire]], to its prestigious list of [[World Heritage Sites]]. In choosing this area that includes the French ''[[département in France|département]]s'' of [[Loiret]], [[Loir-et-Cher]], [[Indre-et-Loire]], and [[Maine-et-Loire]], the committee said that the Loire Valley is:
&quot;an exceptional cultural landscape, of great beauty, comprised of historic cities and villages, great architectural monuments - the Châteaux - and lands that have been cultivated and shaped by centuries of interaction between local populations and their physical environment, in particular the Loire itself.&quot;

==See also==
* [[Loire River]]
* [[French Wine]]
* [[Châteaux of the Loire Valley]]

==External links==
