        <username>Rschen7754</username>
        <id>210954</id>
      </contributor>
      <comment>{{New-Jersey-road-stub}}</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">[[Image:Circle sign 138.svg|right|150px]]
'''New Jersey State Highway 138''' is state highway in [[New Jersey]]. It is an eastern extension of [[Interstate 195 (New Jersey)|Interstate 195]] (See [[Interstate 95]]) towards [[Belmar, New Jersey]]. Its western terminus is at [[New Jersey State Highway 34]] and [[Interstate 195 (New Jersey)|Interstate 195]] in [[Wall Township, New Jersey]]; its eastern terminus is at [[New Jersey State Highway 35]] in Wall. It was first built as part of [[New Jersey State Highway 38]] in [[1941]] and renumbered &quot;138&quot; in 1989 when it became clear that the gap between two sections of [[Route 38 (New Jersey)|Route 38]] would not be filled.  Although [[Interstate 195 (New Jersey)|Interstate 195]] ends at [[Route 34 (New Jersey)|Route 34]], Route 138 carries another exit for it (Exit 36).  The traffic lights on Route 138 often cause congestion during peak hours because of Route 18's premature ending, and it is also meant to be an evacuation route in case of a disaster.  The length of the highway is 3.5 miles.


{{New-Jersey-road-stub}}
{{njsr box|before=133|beforeother=|title=138|after=139|afterother=}}

[[Category:State Routes in New Jersey|138]]</text>
