      <text xml:space="preserve">In [[Greek mythology]], '''Eetion''' was the father of [[Andromache]] and seven sons, including Podes who was killed by [[Menelaus]] in the Trojan War (Book 17, Iliad). He was King of [[Thebe, Cilicia|Thebe]] in [[Cilicia]].

Another '''Eetion''', also mentioned in the Iliad, ruled over the island of [[Imbros]].
{{greek-myth-stub}}

[[Category:Greek mythology]]</text>
