  <page>
    <title>Metacharacter</title>
    <id>81959</id>
    <revision>
      <id>15973482</id>
      <timestamp>2005-05-08T06:06:48Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <username>Demi</username>
        <id>128150</id>
      </contributor>
      <comment>fix categorization, expand a bit</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">A '''metacharacter''' is a character that has a special meaning instead of a [[literal]] meaning to a computer program, such as a [[Operating system shell|shell interpreter]] or a [[regular expression]] engine.

== Examples ==

*In some [[Unix shell]]s, the &lt;tt&gt;;&lt;/tt&gt; (semicolon) character stops the previous statement and starts a new one.
*In many regular expression engines, the &lt;tt&gt;.&lt;/tt&gt; (dot) character matches any character, not just a dot.
*In [[XML]] and [[HTML]], the &lt;tt&gt;&amp;&lt;/tt&gt; (ampersand) character introduces an [[Character encodings in HTML|HTML entity]].

{{Compu-stub}}</text>
    </revision>
