  <page>
    <title>Androgeus</title>
    <id>81965</id>
    <revision>
      <id>22457491</id>
      <timestamp>2005-09-03T08:03:55Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <username>YurikBot</username>
        <id>271058</id>
      </contributor>
      <minor />
      <comment>robot  Adding: bg, uk</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">In [[Greek mythology]], '''Androgeus''' was the father of [[Sthenelus]] and a son of [[Minos]] and [[Pasiphae]].

[[Aegeus]], [[King of Athens]], killed Androgeus because he won every prize during a feast.  As punishment, the [[Athens|Athenians]] had to send several youths every year to be devoured by the [[Minotaur]].  This continued until the Minotaur was killed by [[Theseus]].

Alternative: Andregeos

[[Category:Greek mythological people]]
----

Another Androgeus was [[King of the Britons]], see: [[Androgeus of Britain]]

[[bg:Андрогей]]
[[it:Androgeo]]
[[uk:Андрогей]]</text>
