      </contributor>
      <text xml:space="preserve">In [[Greek mythology]], '''Oileus''', or '''Oïleus''' was the King of [[Locris]].  His father was given as [[Odoedocus]] (whom Ajax succeeded as King of Locris) and his mother as Agrianome (otherwise unknown).  Oileus's wife was [[Eriopis]], who bore him a son named [[Ajax the lesser|Ajax]].  Oileus was also the father of [[Medon]], who is usually regarded as illegitimate; Medon's mother was said to be a nymph named Rhene, not Eriopis.  Oileus was also an [[Argonauts|Argonaut]].

{{greek-myth-stub}}

[[Category:Argonauts]]

[[bg:Оилей]]</text>
