      <text xml:space="preserve">:''For other defintions, consult [[Stentor (disambiguation)]].''

In [[Greek mythology]], '''Stentor''' (&amp;Sigma;&amp;tau;&amp;epsilon;&amp;nu;&amp;tau;&amp;omega;&amp;rho;) was a herald on the Greek side during the [[Trojan War]].  His name has given rise to the adjective &quot;stentorian&quot;, meaning loud-voiced, for which he was famous.  [[Homer]] said his &quot;''voice was as powerful as fifty voices of other men.''&quot; He died after his defeat by [[Hermes]] in a shouting contest.  See the ''[[Iliad]]'', V, 783.

[[Category:People who fought in the Trojan War]]

[[de:Stentor]]
[[fr:Stentor]]
[[pl:Stentor]]</text>
