      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Polybus''' was a famous physician.  See [[History of anatomy]].

-----
In [[Greek mythology]], there were four people named '''Polybus''', or '''Pólybos'''.

#A [[Corinth, Greece|Corinthian]] king, husband of [[Merope]] or [[Periboea]], who raised [[Oedipus]], who had been abandoned by his mother.
#A King of [[Sicyon]], father of [[Talaus]].
#A King of [[Thebes (Egypt)|Thebes]] (in [[Egypt]]).  [[Menelaus]] and [[Helen of Troy|Helen]] stayed in his court for a while after the [[Trojan War]].
#A suitor of [[Penelope]], killed by [[Eumaeus]],
[[Category:Greek mythological people]] [[Category:Ancient Greek physicians]]

{{Greek-myth-stub}}</text>
    </revision>
