  <page>
    <title>Talaus</title>
    <id>82012</id>
    <revision>
      <id>20836280</id>
      <timestamp>2005-08-12T07:27:06Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <username>GeeJo</username>
        <id>296804</id>
      </contributor>
      <text xml:space="preserve">In [[Greek mythology]], '''Talaus''' was King of [[Argos]] and was one of the [[Argonauts]].  He was the son of [[Polybus]] and [[Tyro]] (or [[Bias (mythology)|Bias]] and [[Pero]]).  His wife is alternately said to be [[Lysimache]], [[Eurynome]] or [[Lysianassa]].  He was father of [[Adrastus]], and possibly of [[Aristomachus]], [[Astynome]], [[Eriphyle]], [[Hippomedan]], [[Mecistus]], [[Metidice]], [[Parthinopaeus]] and/or [[Pronax]].

{{greek-myth-stub}}

[[Category:Argonauts]]</text>
