      <text xml:space="preserve">&lt;div style=&quot;float:right&quot;&gt;[[Image:California map showing Merced County.png]]&lt;/div&gt;
'''Merced County''' is a [[county]] located in [[California]]'s [[California Central Valley|Central Valley]], north of [[Fresno, California|Fresno]] and southeast of [[San Jose, California|San Jose]].  As of [[2000]] the population was 210,554.  The county seat is [[Merced, California|Merced]].  The county is named after the [[Merced River]].

==History==
Merced County was formed in [[1855]] from parts of [[Mariposa County, California|Mariposa County]].  Parts of its territory were given to [[Fresno County, California|Fresno County]] in [[1856]].

The county derives its name from the [[Merced River]], or ''El R&amp;iacute;o de Nuestra Se&amp;ntilde;ora de la Merced'' (River of Our Lady of Mercy); named in [[1806]] by an expedition, headed by [[Gabriel Moraga]], which came upon it at the end of a hot dusty ride.

== Geography ==
According to the [[United States Census Bureau|U.S. Census Bureau]], the county has a total area of 5,107 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (1,972 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  4,995 km&amp;sup2; (1,929 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 112 km&amp;sup2; (43 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is water.  The total area is 2.19% water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]][[Geographic references#2|&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;]] of [[2000]], there are 210,554 people, 63,815 households, and 49,775 families residing in the county.  The [[population density]] is 42/km&amp;sup2; (109/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 68,373 housing units at an average density of 14/km&amp;sup2; (36/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the county is 56.21% [[Race (U.S. census)|White]], 3.83% [[Race (U.S. census)|Black]] or [[Race (U.S. census)|African American]], 1.19% [[Race (U.S. census)|Native American]], 6.80% [[Race (U.S. census)|Asian]], 0.19% [[Race (U.S. census)|Pacific Islander]], 26.13% from [[race (U.S. census)|other races]], and 5.65% from two or more races.  45.34% of the population are [[Race (U.S. census)|Hispanic]] or [[Race (U.S. census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 63,815 households out of which 45.40% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 57.80% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 14.10% have a female householder with no husband present, and 22.00% are non-families. 17.70% of all households are made up of individuals and 7.40% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 3.25 and the average family size is 3.69.

In the county the population is spread out with 34.50% under the age of 18, 10.30% from 18 to 24, 27.90% from 25 to 44, 17.80% from 45 to 64, and 9.50% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 29 years.  For every 100 females there are 99.30 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 96.60 males.

The median income for a household in the county is $35,532, and the median income for a family is $38,009. Males have a median income of $31,721 versus $23,911 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the county is $14,257.  21.70% of the population and 16.90% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 28.40% of those under the age of 18 and 10.70% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

