      <text xml:space="preserve">&lt;div style=&quot;float:right&quot;&gt;[[Image:California map showing Placer County.png]]&lt;/div&gt;
'''Placer County''' is a [[county]] located in [[California]], USA's [[Sierra Nevada (US)|Sierra Nevada]], in the [[Gold Country]].  It stretches from the suburbs of [[Sacramento, California|Sacramento]] to [[Lake Tahoe]] and the [[Nevada]] border.  Because of the expansion of the Sacramento metropolitan area, Placer County is one of the fastest growing counties in the state.  As of [[2000]], the population was 248,399.  In [[2004]], the population had grown to 307,004.  The [[county seat]] is [[Auburn, California|Auburn]].

==History==
Placer County was created from parts of [[Sutter County, California|Sutter]] and [[Yuba County, California|Yuba]] Counties in [[1851]].

&quot;Placer&quot; is probably a contraction of the words ''plaza de oro'' (the place of [[gold]]) and in [[Spanish language|Spanish]] means &quot;a place near a river where gold is found.&quot; The county derived its name from the numerous places where the method of extracting gold from the earth, called [[placer mining]], was practiced.

== Geography ==
According to the [[United States Census Bureau|U.S. Census Bureau]], the county has a total area of 3,892 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (1,503 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  3,637 km&amp;sup2; (1,404 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 255 km&amp;sup2; (98 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is water.  The total area is 6.55% water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]][[Geographic references#2|&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;]] of [[2000]], there are 248,399 people, 93,382 households, and 67,701 families residing in the county.  The [[population density]] is 68/km&amp;sup2; (177/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 107,302 housing units at an average density of 30/km&amp;sup2; (76/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the county is 88.59% [[Race (U.S. census)|White]], 0.82% [[Race (U.S. census)|Black]] or [[Race (U.S. census)|African American]], 0.89% [[Race (U.S. census)|Native American]], 2.95% [[Race (U.S. census)|Asian]], 0.16% [[Race (U.S. census)|Pacific Islander]], 3.39% from [[race (U.S. census)|other races]], and 3.21% from two or more races.  9.67% of the population are [[Race (U.S. census)|Hispanic]] or [[Race (U.S. census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 93,382 households out of which 35.30% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 59.40% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 9.20% have a female householder with no husband present, and 27.50% are non-families. 21.30% of all households are made up of individuals and 8.10% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.63 and the average family size is 3.06.

In the county the population is spread out with 26.50% under the age of 18, 6.90% from 18 to 24, 29.00% from 25 to 44, 24.50% from 45 to 64, and 13.10% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 38 years.  For every 100 females there are 96.40 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 93.90 males.

The median income for a household in the county is $57,535, and the median income for a family is $65,858. Males have a median income of $50,410 versus $33,763 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the county is $27,963.  5.80% of the population and 3.90% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 6.30% of those under the age of 18 and 3.80% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

