    <title>Plumas County, California</title>
    <id>82034</id>
    <revision>
      <id>38463285</id>
      <timestamp>2006-02-06T14:17:20Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <username>Ben W Bell</username>
        <id>73920</id>
      </contributor>
      <comment>Don't presume the reader is American, state that it is in the US in the opening line.</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">&lt;div style=&quot;float:right&quot;&gt;[[Image:California map showing Plumas County.png]]&lt;/div&gt;
'''Plumas County''' is a [[county]] located in [[California]]'s [[Sierra Nevada (US)|Sierra Nevada]] in the [[United States]].  The county gets its name from the [[Spanish language|Spanish]] words for the [[Feather River]] (''Rio de las Plumas''), which flows through the county.  As of [[2000]], the population is 20,824.  The [[county seat]] is [[Quincy, California|Quincy]].

The only incorported city in the county is [[Portola, California|Portola]].

==History==
Plumas County was formed from parts of [[Butte County, California|Butte County]] in [[1854]].  Parts of the county's territory were given to [[Lassen County, California|Lassen County]] in [[1864]].

The [[Spain|Spanish]] originally called one of the tributaries of the [[Sacramento River]] ''El Rio de las Plumas'' or the &quot;River of Feathers.&quot; The Legislature, in creating this county, gave it the name &quot;Plumas&quot; because all of the numerous branches of the [[Feather River]] have their origins in its mountains.

== Geography ==
According to the [[United States Census Bureau|U.S. Census Bureau]], the county has a total area of 6,769 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (2,613 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  6,614 km&amp;sup2; (2,554 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 155 km&amp;sup2; (60 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is water.  The total area is 2.29% water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]][[Geographic references#2|&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;]] of [[2000]], there are 20,824 people, 9,000 households, and 6,047 families residing in the county.  The [[population density]] is 3/km&amp;sup2; (8/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 13,386 housing units at an average density of 2/km&amp;sup2; (5/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the county is 91.78% [[Race (U.S. census)|White]], 0.62% [[Race (U.S. census)|Black]] or [[Race (U.S. census)|African American]], 2.55% [[Race (U.S. census)|Native American]], 0.53% [[Race (U.S. census)|Asian]], 0.10% [[Race (U.S. census)|Pacific Islander]], 1.81% from [[race (U.S. census)|other races]], and 2.61% from two or more races.  5.65% of the population are [[Race (U.S. census)|Hispanic]] or [[Race (U.S. census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 9,000 households out of which 26.40% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 55.40% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 8.00% have a female householder with no husband present, and 32.80% are non-families. 27.50% of all households are made up of individuals and 10.10% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.29 and the average family size is 2.77.

In the county the population is spread out with 22.70% under the age of 18, 6.00% from 18 to 24, 22.60% from 25 to 44, 30.80% from 45 to 64, and 17.90% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 44 years.  For every 100 females there are 99.80 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 97.90 males.

The median income for a household in the county is $36,351, and the median income for a family is $46,119. Males have a median income of $38,742 versus $25,734 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the county is $19,391.  13.10% of the population and 9.00% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 16.70% of those under the age of 18 and 6.40% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

