  <page>
    <title>Château de Cheverny</title>
    <id>82036</id>
    <revision>
      <id>38392231</id>
      <timestamp>2006-02-06T01:02:07Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <ip>63.153.26.30</ip>
      </contributor>
      <text xml:space="preserve">[[image:Cheverny.jpg|thumb|280px|right|Château de Cheverny]]

The '''[[Château]] de Cheverny''' is located at [[Cheverny]], in the ''[[Département in France|département]]'' of [[Loir-et-Cher]] in the [[Loire Valley]] in [[France]]. The lands were purchased by Henri Hurault, Comte de Cheverny, and Treasurer for War under [[Louis XI of France|King Louis XI]]

Lost to the Crown because of fraud to the State,  it was donated by [[Henry II of France|King Henri II]] to his mistress [[Diane de Poitiers]].  However, she preferred [[Château de Chenonceau]] and sold the property to the former owner's son, Philippe Hurault, who built the château between [[1624]] and [[1630]]. 

During the next 150 years ownership changed many times and in [[1765]] a major interior renovation was undertaken. Required to forfeit much of the Hurault wealth at the time of the [[French Revolution]], the family sold it in [[1802]] but bought it back in [[1824]].

In [[1914]], the owner opened the chateau to the public, one of the first to ever do so. The family still operates it, and Château Cheverny remains a top tourist attraction to this day, renowned for magnificent interior rooms and its collection of furniture, tapestries, and ''objets d'art.''  Around 90 hunting dogs are also kept on the grounds and are taken out for hunts twice weekly.

The Belgian [[comic book]] creator [[Hergé]] used Cheverny as a model for his fictional &quot;''Château de Moulinsart''&quot; (''[[Marlinspike (comics)|Marlinspike]] Hall'' in English) in the ''[[Tintin]]'' books.

[[Category:Castles in France|Cheverny]]
[[Category:Baroque architecture]]
[[Category:Loir-et-Cher]]

[[de:Schloss Cheverny]]
[[fr:Château de Cheverny]]
[[nl:Kasteel van Cheverny]]
[[pl:Zamek w Cheverny]]</text>
    </revision>
