'''San Benito County''' is a [[county]] located in the [[California]] [[Coast Range]] Mountains south of [[San Jose, California|San Jose]].  As of [[2000]] the population was 53,234.  The [[county seat]] is [[Hollister, California|Hollister]].

As housing costs have gone up in the [[San Francisco Bay Area]], commuters have begun moving to San Benito County.

==History==
San Benito County was formed from parts of [[Monterey County, California|Monterey County]] in [[1874]].

The county is named after the San Benito Valley. Father [[Juan Crespi]], in his expedition in [[1772]], named a small river in honor of San Benidicto ([[Benedict of Nursia|Saint Benedict]]), the patron saint of the married, and it is from the contraction of this name that the county took its name.

== Geography ==
According to the [[United States Census Bureau|U.S. Census Bureau]], the county has a total area of 3,602 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (1,391 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  3,598 km&amp;sup2; (1,389 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 4 km&amp;sup2; (2 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is water.  The total area is 0.12% water.

===Adjacent counties===
*[[Santa Clara County, California|Santa Clara County]] — north/northwest
*[[Merced County, California|Merced County]] — northeast
*[[Fresno County, California|Fresno County]] — east/southeast
*[[Monterey County, California|Monterey County]] — southwest/west
*[[Santa Cruz County, California|Santa Cruz County]] — northwest

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]][[Geographic references#2|&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;]] of [[2000]], there are 53,234 people, 15,885 households, and 12,898 families residing in the county.  The [[population density]] is 15/km&amp;sup2; (38/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 16,499 housing units at an average density of 5/km&amp;sup2; (12/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the county is 65.17% [[Race (U.S. census)|White]], 1.08% [[Race (U.S. census)|Black]] or [[Race (U.S. census)|African American]], 1.16% [[Race (U.S. census)|Native American]], 2.40% [[Race (U.S. census)|Asian]], 0.19% [[Race (U.S. census)|Pacific Islander]], 24.87% from [[race (U.S. census)|other races]], and 5.14% from two or more races.  47.93% of the population are [[Race (U.S. census)|Hispanic]] or [[Race (U.S. census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 15,885 households out of which 46.30% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 65.70% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 10.50% have a female householder with no husband present, and 18.80% are non-families. 14.10% of all households are made up of individuals and 5.40% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 3.32 and the average family size is 3.64.

In the county the population is spread out with 32.20% under the age of 18, 8.80% from 18 to 24, 31.50% from 25 to 44, 19.30% from 45 to 64, and 8.10% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 31 years.  For every 100 females there are 102.50 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 99.60 males.

The median income for a household in the county is $57,469, and the median income for a family is $60,665. Males have a median income of $44,158 versus $29,524 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the county is $20,932.  10.00% of the population and 6.70% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 11.40% of those under the age of 18 and 8.50% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

== Cities and towns ==
*[[Hollister, California|Hollister]]
*[[Ridgemark, California|Ridgemark]]
*[[San Juan Bautista, California|San Juan Bautista]]

