'''San Diego County''' is a [[county]] located on the [[Pacific Ocean]] in the far southwest of the [[U.S. state]] of [[California]], along its border with [[Mexico]].  With a population of 3,051,280 (as of [[2005]]), it is the third largest county by population in the state.  The [[county seat]] is the [[city]] of [[San Diego, California|San Diego]].

The San Diego area is one of the fastest growing areas in the state.

==History==
European settlement in what is now San Diego County began with the founding of the [[Mission San Diego de Alcala]] by the [[Spain|Spanish]], in [[1769]].

San Diego County was one of the original counties of California, and was created at the time of statehood in [[1850]].  It was named after [[San Diego Bay]], which had been rechristened in [[1602]] by [[Sebastián Vizcaíno]] in honor of the [[Franciscan]] [[Didacus of Alcalá|St. Didacus of Alcalá]], known in [[Spanish language|Spanish]] as San Diego de Alcalá de Henares, and whose name was borne by Vizcaíno's flagship.

Parts of the county were later divided off to create [[Riverside County, California|Riverside County]], in [[1893]], and [[Imperial County, California|Imperial County]], in [[1907]].

==Geography==
According to the [[United States Census Bureau|U.S. Census Bureau]], the county has a total area of 11,721 [[square kilometer|km²]] (4,526 [[square mile|mi²]]).  10,878 km² (4,200 mi²) of it is land and 843 km² (326 mi²) of it is water.  The total area is 7.20% water.

San Diego County has varied topography. On its western side is seventy miles of coastline. Snow-capped mountains rise to the northeast, with the [[Sonoran Desert]] to the far east. The [[Cleveland National Forest]] lies to the southeast.

[[North San Diego County, California|North San Diego County]] is known locally as &quot;North County&quot;, and has a culture of its own.

=== Adjacent Counties ===
** [[Imperial County, California]] -  (east)
** [[Orange County, California]] -  (northwest)
** [[Riverside County, California]] -  (north)

== Sites of interest ==

===Observatories===
**[[Mount Laguna Observatory]] - owned and operated by [[San Diego State University]] ([[San Diego State University|SDSU]])
**[[Palomar Observatory]] - owned and primarily operated by [[California Institute of Technology]] ([[CalTech]])

===Wine regions===
*the [[Ramona Valley]] wine-producing region is located 28 [[mile]]s (45 [[Kilometre|km]]) northeast of [[San Diego, California|San Diego]]

