    <title>Eumelus</title>
    <id>82051</id>
    <revision>
      <id>20022016</id>
      <timestamp>2005-08-01T02:44:34Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <username>GeeJo</username>
        <id>296804</id>
      </contributor>
      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Eumelus''' was the name of several men in [[Greek mythology]]:
#A Eumelus succeeded [[Adrastus]] as the King of [[Pherae]].  He led Pherae and [[Iolcus]] in the [[Trojan War]] on the side of the Greeks.
#Another Eumeleus was the husband of [[Ipthime]] and the son of [[Admetus]] and [[Alcestis]].  He won the chariot races at [[Achilles]]'s funeral.
#Still another Eumeleus was the father of [[Antheias]].

{{Greek-myth-stub}}

[[Category:Greek mythological people]]
[[Category:People who fought in the Trojan War]]</text>
    </revision>
