  <page>
    <title>San Joaquin County, California</title>
    <id>82055</id>
    <revision>
      <id>40489758</id>
      <timestamp>2006-02-20T23:12:04Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <username>Rich Farmbrough</username>
        <id>82835</id>
      </contributor>
      <minor />
      <comment>External links per MoS.</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">&lt;div style=&quot;float:right&quot;&gt;[[Image:California map showing San Joaquin County.png]]&lt;/div&gt;
'''San Joaquin County''' is a [[county]] located in the [[United States of America]] in [[California]]'s [[California Central Valley|Central Valley]], just east of the [[San Francisco Bay Area]].  Many Bay Area commuters have moved into the county because of cheaper housing costs.  As of [[2006]], the population is approx. 620,000.  The [[county seat]] is [[Stockton, California|Stockton]].

Stockton is a deep water port on the [[San Joaquin River]].

==History==
San Joaquin County was one of the original counties of California, created in [[1850]] at the time of statehood.

The county takes its name from the [[San Joaquin River]]. In the early [[1800s]] Lieutenant [[Gabriel Moraga]], commanding an expedition in the lower great [[California Central Valley]], gave the name of ''San Joaquin'' (meaning Saint [[Joachim]]) to a rivulet that springs from the [[Sierra Nevada (US)|Sierra Nevada]] and empties into [[Buena Vista Lake]].

== Geography ==
According to the [[United States Census Bureau|U.S. Census Bureau]], the county has a total area of 3,694 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (1,426 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  3,624 km&amp;sup2; (1,399 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 70 km&amp;sup2; (27 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is water.  The total area is 1.89% water.

===Major highways===
*[[Interstate 5]]
*[[Interstate 205 (California)|Interstate 205]]
*[[Interstate 580 (California)|Interstate 580]]
*[[California State Highway 99]]
*[[California State Route 4]] (Crosstown Freeway/California Delta Highway)
*[[California State Route 120]]

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]][[Geographic references#2|&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;]] of [[2000]], there are 563,598 people, 181,629 households, and 134,768 families residing in the county.  The [[population density]] is 156/km&amp;sup2; (403/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 189,160 housing units at an average density of 52/km&amp;sup2; (135/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the county is 58.13% [[Race (U.S. census)|White]], 6.69% [[Race (U.S. census)|Black]] or [[Race (U.S. census)|African American]], 1.13% [[Race (U.S. census)|Native American]], 11.41% [[Race (U.S. census)|Asian]], 0.35% [[Race (U.S. census)|Pacific Islander]], 16.26% from [[race (U.S. census)|other races]], and 6.05% from two or more races.  30.53% of the population are [[Race (U.S. census)|Hispanic]] or [[Race (U.S. census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 181,629 households out of which 40.50% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 54.30% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 14.00% have a female householder with no husband present, and 25.80% are non-families. 20.70% of all households are made up of individuals and 8.40% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 3.00 and the average family size is 3.48.

In the county the population is spread out with 31.00% under the age of 18, 10.00% from 18 to 24, 28.80% from 25 to 44, 19.60% from 45 to 64, and 10.60% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 32 years.  For every 100 females there are 99.90 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 97.20 males.

The median income for a household in the county is $41,282, and the median income for a family is $46,919. Males have a median income of $39,246 versus $27,507 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the county is $17,365.  17.70% of the population and 13.50% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 23.70% of those under the age of 18 and 10.00% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

== Cities, towns, and communities ==
*[[August, California|August]]
*[[Country Club, California|Country Club]]
*[[Escalon, California|Escalon]]
*[[Farmington, California|Farmington]]
*[[French Camp, California|French Camp]]
*[[Garden Acres, California|Garden Acres]]
*[[Kennedy, California|Kennedy]]
*[[Lathrop, California|Lathrop]]
*[[Lincoln Village, California|Lincoln Village]]
*[[Linden, California|Linden]]
*[[Lockeford, California|Lockeford]]
*[[Lodi, California|Lodi]]
*[[Manteca, California|Manteca]]
*[[Morada, California|Morada]]
*[[Mountain House, California|Mountain House]]
*[[North Woodbridge, California|North Woodbridge]]
*[[Ripon, California|Ripon]]
*[[South Woodbridge, California|South Woodbridge]]
*[[Stockton, California|Stockton]]
*[[Taft Mosswood, California|Taft Mosswood]]
*[[Tracy, California|Tracy]]

==See also==
*[[List of school districts in San Joaquin County, California]]

==External links==
*[http://www.co.san-joaquin.ca.us San Joaquin County official website]
*[http://www.stocktoncourt.org San Joaquin County Superior Court]

