'''Santa Clara County''' is a [[county]] located in [[California]]'s [[San Francisco Bay Area]].  It is the site of [[Silicon Valley]].  As of [[2000]] it had a population of 1,682,585.  The [[county seat]] is [[San Jose, California|San Jose]].

==History==
Santa Clara County was one of the original counties of California, formed in [[1850]] at the time of statehood.  Part of the county's territory was given to [[Alameda County, California|Alameda County]] in [[1853]].

The county is named after [[Mission Santa Clara de Asis|Mission Santa Clara]], which was established in [[1777]], and named for [[Clare of Assisi|Saint Clare of Assisi]], [[Italy]]. The name &quot;Clare&quot; or &quot;Clara&quot; means &quot;clear&quot; or &quot;bright.&quot;

In [[1882]], Santa Clara County tried to levy taxes upon property of the [[Southern Pacific Railroad]] within county boundaries.  The result was the [[U.S. Supreme Court]] case of ''[[Santa Clara County v. Southern Pacific Railroad]]'', [[Case citation|118 U.S. 394]] ([[1886]]), in which the Court established the doctrine of [[corporate personhood]].

== Geography ==
According to the [[United States Census Bureau|U.S. Census Bureau]], the county has a total area of 3,377 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (1,304 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  3,343 km&amp;sup2; (1,291 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 34 km&amp;sup2; (13 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is water.  The total area is 1.02% water.

The county is bordered to the north-west by
[[San Mateo County, California|San Mateo County]], to the
south-west by [[Santa Cruz County, California | Santa Cruz County]], to the north by [[Alameda County, California | Alameda County]],
to the east by [[Stanislaus County, California|Stanislaus County]], to the south-east by [[Merced County, California | Merced County]],
and to the south by [[San Benito County, California | San Benito County]].

The [[San Andreas Fault]] runs along the [[Santa Cruz Mountains]] in the
south of the county.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]][[Geographic references#2|&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;]] of [[2000]], there are 1,682,585 people, 565,863 households, and 395,538 families residing in the county.  The [[population density]] is 503/km&amp;sup2; (1,304/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 579,329 housing units at an average density of 173/km&amp;sup2; (449/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the county is 53.83% [[Race (U.S. census)|White]], 2.80% [[Race (U.S. census)|Black]] or [[Race (U.S. census)|African American]], 0.67% [[Race (U.S. census)|Native American]], 25.56% [[Race (U.S. census)|Asian]], 0.34% [[Race (U.S. census)|Pacific Islander]], 12.13% from [[race (U.S. census)|other races]], and 4.66% from two or more races.  23.98% of the population are [[Race (U.S. census)|Hispanic]] or [[Race (U.S. census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 565,863 households out of which 34.90% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 54.90% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 10.00% have a female householder with no husband present, and 30.10% are non-families. 21.40% of all households are made up of individuals and 5.90% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.92 and the average family size is 3.41.

In the county the population is spread out with 24.70% under the age of 18, 9.30% from 18 to 24, 35.40% from 25 to 44, 21.00% from 45 to 64, and 9.50% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 34 years.  For every 100 females there are 102.80 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 101.90 males.

The median income for a household in the county is $74,335, and the median income for a family is $81,717. Males have a median income of $56,240 versus $40,574 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the county is $32,795.  7.50% of the population and 4.90% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 8.40% of those under the age of 18 and 6.40% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

Santa Clara County has the [[Richest counties in the United States|highest median household income]] of any county in California.

==Politics==
