  <page>
    <title>Shasta County, California</title>
    <id>82097</id>
    <revision>
      <id>40222750</id>
      <timestamp>2006-02-19T01:39:27Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <username>Prsephone1674</username>
        <id>97846</id>
      </contributor>
      <minor />
      <comment>/* Cities and towns */ Bad link repair ([[Wikipedia:Bad links|You can help!]])</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">&lt;div style=&quot;float:right&quot;&gt;[[Image:California map showing Shasta County.png]]&lt;/div&gt;
'''Shasta County''' is a [[county]] located in northern [[California]], [[United States|USA]], in the [[Cascade Range|Cascade Mountains]].  As of [[2000]] the population was 163,256.  The [[county seat]] is [[Redding, California|Redding]].

Shasta County is the home of [[Lassen Peak]], [[Shasta Lake]], and the [[Lassen Volcanic National Park]].

==History==
Shasta County was one of the original counties of California, created in [[1850]] at the time of statehood.  Parts of the county's territory were given to [[Siskiyou County, California|Siskiyou County]] in [[1852]], and to [[Tehama County, California|Tehama County]] in [[1856]].

The county was named after [[Mount Shasta]]; the name &quot;Shasta&quot; is derived from the [[English language|English]] equivalent for the name of an Indian tribe that once lived in the area. The name of the tribe was spelled in various ways until the present version was used when the county was established. Originally Mt. Shasta was within the county, but it is now part of Siskiyou County, to the north. Its 14,162-foot peak is visible throughout most of the county.

== Geography ==
According to the [[United States Census Bureau|U.S. Census Bureau]], the county has a total area of 9,965 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (3,847 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  9,804 km&amp;sup2; (3,785 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 161 km&amp;sup2; (62 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is water.  The total area is 1.62% water. Mountains line the county on the east, north and west. The Sacramento River flows out of the mountains to the north, through the center of the county, and toward the Sacramento Valley to the south.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]][[Geographic references#2|&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;]] of [[2000]], there are 163,256 people, 63,426 households, and 44,017 families residing in the county.  The [[population density]] is 17/km&amp;sup2; (43/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 68,810 housing units at an average density of 7/km&amp;sup2; (18/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the county is 89.32% [[Race (U.S. census)|White]], 0.75% [[Race (U.S. census)|Black]] or [[Race (U.S. census)|African American]], 2.77% [[Race (U.S. census)|Native American]], 1.87% [[Race (U.S. census)|Asian]], 0.11% [[Race (U.S. census)|Pacific Islander]], 1.71% from [[race (U.S. census)|other races]], and 3.47% from two or more races.  5.51% of the population are [[Race (U.S. census)|Hispanic]] or [[Race (U.S. census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 63,426 households out of which 31.70% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 53.00% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 11.90% have a female householder with no husband present, and 30.60% are non-families. 24.70% of all households are made up of individuals and 10.20% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.52 and the average family size is 2.98.

In the county the population is spread out with 26.10% under the age of 18, 8.20% from 18 to 24, 25.30% from 25 to 44, 25.20% from 45 to 64, and 15.20% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 39 years.  For every 100 females there are 95.10 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 91.20 males.

The median income for a household in the county is $34,335, and the median income for a family is $40,491. Males have a median income of $35,959 versus $24,773 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the county is $17,738.  15.40% of the population and 11.30% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 21.00% of those under the age of 18 and 7.30% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

==Annual Events==
 
*Kool April Nites (April) &amp;mdash; A Classic Car Show 
*Rodeo Week Festivities (May) 
*Art Fair and Fiddler’s Jamboree (May)
*Whiskeytown Regatta (May)
*Redding Exchange Club Air Show (June)
*Shasta District Fair (June) &amp;mdash; The County fair
*Fourth of July Fireworks Celebration (July)
*Burney Basin Days (July)
*Intermountain Fair (September)  

== Cities and towns ==
*[[Anderson, California|Anderson]]
*[[Big Bend, California|Big Bend]]
*[[Burney, California|Burney]]
*[[Cottonwood, California|Cottonwood]]
*[[Fall River Mills, California|Fall River Mills]]
*[[French Gulch, California|French Gulch]]
*[[Lakehead-Lakeshore, California|Lakehead-Lakeshore]]
*[[McArthur, California|McArthur]]
*[[Millville, California|Millville]]
*[[Montgomery Creek, California|Montgomery Creek]]
*[[Palo Cedro, California|Palo Cedro]]
*[[Redding, California|Redding]]
*[[Round Mountain, California|Round Mountain]]
*[[Shasta Lake, California|Shasta Lake]]
*[[Shingletown, California|Shingletown]]
*[[Ono, California|Ono]]
*[[Igo, California|Igo]]
*[[Platina, California|Platina]]

Of these places, Redding, Shasta Lake, and Anderson are the only incorporated areas.

==Education and Housing==

===Colleges and Universities===

Shasta County has four colleges and universities:
:Shasta College, Redding – 2 year, fully accredited
:Simpson College, Redding – 4 year, fully accredited
:National University, Redding – 4 year, fully accredited
:Shasta Bible College - 4 year  

===High Schools and Below===
*43 Elementary Schools
*10 Junior High Schools
*8 High Schools
*35 Private Schools

===Housing===
*Median price for a house is about $128,000.
*Median rental rate is $500/month.

== Points of interest ==
* [[Lassen Peak]]
* [[Lassen Volcanic National Park]]
* [[Shasta Lake]]
* [[Turtle Bay Exploration Park]]
* [[Hat Creek Radio Observatory]]

==See also==
*[[List of school districts in Shasta County, California]]

==External links==
*[http://www.co.shasta.ca.us/ County of Shasta official website]
*[http://www.UntraveledRoad.com/USA/California/Shasta.htm Photographic virtual tour of Shasta County]
*[http://www.shastahistorical.org Shasta Historical Society] &amp;mdash; A large database of historical county photographs

{{Cities of Shasta County, California}}
{{California}}
[[Category:Shasta County, California| ]]
[[Category:California counties]]

[[bg:Шаста]]
[[fr:Comté de Shasta]]
[[pt:Condado de Shasta]]</text>
    </revision>
