      <text xml:space="preserve">The name '''Aetheria''' may refer to&amp;mdash;
*''in [[Greek mythology]]'', one of the [[Heliades]], daughters of [[Helios]], the [[solar deity|sun god]].
*a [[Egeria (nun)|nun living in the late fourth century]], also known as '''Etheria''', '''Eucheria''', or '''Egeria'''.  She is known for having gone on a [[pilgrimage]] to the [[Holy Land]], and wrote an account of her travels called the ''Peregrinatio Ætheriæ''.

