      <text xml:space="preserve">&lt;div style=&quot;float:right&quot;&gt;[[Image:California map showing Solano County.png]]&lt;/div&gt;
'''Solano County''' is a [[county]] located in central part of the [[U.S. state]] of [[California]], about halfway between [[San Francisco, California|San Francisco]] and [[Sacramento, California|Sacramento]] and is one of the nine [[San Francisco Bay Area]] counties.  As of [[2000]] its population was 394,542.  The [[county seat]] is [[Fairfield, California|Fairfield]].

==History==
Solano County was one of the original counties of California, created in [[1850]] at the time of statehood.

The county derives its name indirectly from that of the [[Franciscan]] [[missionary]], Father [[Francisco Solano]], whose name was given in baptism to the chief of one of the [[Native Americans in the United States|Native American]] tribes of the region. Before receiving the name ''Solano'', the chief was called ''Sem-yeto'', which signifies &quot;brave or fierce hand.&quot; At the request of General [[Mariano Vallejo]], the county was named for [[Chief Solano]], who at one time ruled over most of the land and tribes between the [[Petaluma Creek]] and the [[Sacramento River]].

== Geography ==
According to the [[United States Census Bureau|U.S. Census Bureau]], the county has a total area of 2,348 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (907 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  2,148 km&amp;sup2; (829 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 201 km&amp;sup2; (77 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is water.  The total area is 8.55% water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]][[Geographic references#2|&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;]] of [[2000]], there are 394,542 people, 130,403 households, and 97,411 families residing in the county.  The [[population density]] is 184/km&amp;sup2; (476/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 134,513 housing units at an average density of 63/km&amp;sup2; (162/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the county is 56.37% [[Race (U.S. census)|White]], 14.91% [[Race (U.S. census)|Black]] or [[Race (U.S. census)|African American]], 0.79% [[Race (U.S. census)|Native American]], 12.75% [[Race (U.S. census)|Asian]], 0.78% [[Race (U.S. census)|Pacific Islander]], 8.01% from [[race (U.S. census)|other races]], and 6.39% from two or more races.  17.64% of the population are [[Race (U.S. census)|Hispanic]] or [[Race (U.S. census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 130,403 households out of which 39.90% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 55.70% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 13.80% have a female householder with no husband present, and 25.30% are non-families. 19.60% of all households are made up of individuals and 6.50% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.90 and the average family size is 3.33.

In the county the population is spread out with 28.30% under the age of 18, 9.20% from 18 to 24, 31.30% from 25 to 44, 21.70% from 45 to 64, and 9.50% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 34 years.  For every 100 females there are 101.50 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 100.20 males.

The median income for a household in the county is $54,099, and the median income for a family is $60,597. Males have a median income of $41,787 versus $31,916 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the county is $21,731.  8.30% of the population and 6.10% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 10.30% of those under the age of 18 and 6.30% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

