      <minor />
      <comment>disambig</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">&lt;div style=&quot;float:right&quot;&gt;[[Image:California map showing Trinity County.png]]&lt;/div&gt;
'''Trinity County''' is a [[county]] located in northwestern [[California]], along the [[Trinity River (California)|Trinity River]] and among the [[Klamath Mountains]].  As of [[2000]] its population was 13,022.  Its [[county seat]] is [[Weaverville, California|Weaverville]].  There are no incorporated cities in Trinity County.

Trinity County is part of the [[Emerald Triangle]].

Trinity County Government Offices, located in [[Weaverville, California|Weaverville]], can be accessed [http://www.trinitycounty.org here] with visitor and tourism info available at [http://www.trinitycounty.com Trinity County Chamber Of Commerce],[http://www.weavervilleinfo.com Weavervilleinfo] and [http://www.trinitycam.com Trinity Cam]

==History==
Trinity County was one of the original counties of California, created in [[1850]] at the time of statehood.  Parts of the county were given to [[Klamath County, California|Klamath County]] in [[1852]] and to [[Humboldt County, California|Humboldt County]] in [[1853]].  Klamath County ceased to exist in [[1876]].

The county takes its name from the [[Trinity River (California)|Trinity River]], named in [[1845]] by Major [[Pearson B. Reading]], who was under the mistaken impression that the stream emptied into [[Trinidad Bay]]. ''Trinity'' is the [[English language|English]] version of Trinidad.

== Geography ==
According to the [[United States Census Bureau|U.S. Census Bureau]], the county has a total area of 8,307 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (3,208 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  8,233 km&amp;sup2; (3,179 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 75 km&amp;sup2; (29 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is water.  The total area is 0.90% water. The county contains a singificant portion of [[Shasta-Trinity National Forest]], home to the [[Trinity Alps]]. The county hosts many visitors, especially during summer months, for camping, backpacking, and fishing.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]][[Geographic references#2|&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;]] of [[2000]], there are 13,022 people, 5,587 households, and 3,625 families residing in the county.  The [[population density]] is 2/km&amp;sup2; (4/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 7,980 housing units at an average density of 1/km&amp;sup2; (2/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the county is 88.87% [[Race (U.S. census)|White]], 0.45% [[Race (U.S. census)|Black]] or [[Race (U.S. census)|African American]], 4.85% [[Race (U.S. census)|Native American]], 0.47% [[Race (U.S. census)|Asian]], 0.12% [[Race (U.S. census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.88% from [[race (U.S. census)|other races]], and 4.38% from two or more races.  3.97% of the population are [[Race (U.S. census)|Hispanic]] or [[Race (U.S. census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 5,587 households out of which 25.40% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 50.50% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 10.10% have a female householder with no husband present, and 35.10% are non-families. 29.50% of all households are made up of individuals and 11.10% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.29 and the average family size is 2.80.

In the county the population is spread out with 22.80% under the age of 18, 5.10% from 18 to 24, 22.70% from 25 to 44, 32.10% from 45 to 64, and 17.20% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 45 years.  For every 100 females there are 104.20 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 102.60 males.

The median income for a household in the county is $27,711, and the median income for a family is $34,343. Males have a median income of $31,131 versus $24,271 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the county is $16,868.  18.70% of the population and 14.10% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 26.20% of those under the age of 18 and 7.20% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

== Cities and towns ==
*[[Hayfork, California|Hayfork]]
*[[Lewiston, California|Lewiston]]
*[[Weaverville, California|Weaverville]]

==External link==
*[http://www.trinitycounty.org/ Trinity County official website]
[[Category:California counties]]
[[Category:Trinity County, California| ]]
{{California}}

[[bg:Тринити (окръг)]]
[[fr:Comté de Trinity (Californie)]]
[[pt:Condado de Trinity (Califórnia)]]</text>
