      <text xml:space="preserve">{{French commune|nomcommune=Bourges| région=[[Centre (France)|Centre]] |département=[[Cher (département)|Cher]] (''[[préfecture]]'')  | arrondissement=Bourges|canton=Chief town of 5 cantons| insee=18033 |cp=18000 |gentilé=Berruyers |maire=[[Serge Lepeltier]] |mandat=[[2001]]-[[2008]] | intercomm=[[communauté d'agglomération de Bourges|Communauté&lt;br&gt;d'agglomération&lt;br&gt;de Bourges]] | longitude=02° 23' 47&quot; E |latitude=47° 05' 04&quot; N |alt moy=153 m |alt mini=120 m |alt maxi=169 m | hectares=6,874 |km²=68.74 |sans=72,480 |date-sans=1999 |dens=1,054 |date-dens=1999}}

&lt;!-- Image with unknown copyright status removed: [[Image:Gothic.architecture.bourges.1.jpg|thumb|right|250px|The vaulted nave of Bourges Cathedral]] --&gt;
[[Image:BourgesDB362.jpg|thumb|right|250px|Floorplan of the cathedral]]

'''Bourges''' is a town and [[commune in France|commune]] in central [[France]]. It is the ''[[préfecture]]'' (capital) of the ''[[département in France|département]]'' of [[Cher (département)|Cher]], and was also the capital of the former [[provinces of France|province]] of [[Berry (province)|Berry]].

==Geography==

Bourges is located on the [[Yèvre]] river.

==Sights==

[[Cathédrale Saint-Étienne de Bourges|Its Gothic cathedral]] (built [[1195]]&amp;ndash;[[1255]]) was added to the list of the [[World Heritage Sites]] by [[UNESCO]] in [[1992]].

==Colleges and universities==
* [[Ecole des Beaux Arts|École nationale des beaux-arts de Bourges]]

==Miscellaneous==

[[Serge Lepeltier]] became mayor of the city in [[1995]] and again in [[2001]].

The ''[[Printemps de Bourges]]'' music festival takes place in Bourges every year.

The city's name is cognate to the English word [[borough]].

===Twin towns===

Bourges is twinned with:
* [[Augsburg]], [[Germany]]
* [[Aveiro]], [[Portugal]]
* [[Forlì]] , [[Italy]]
* [[Koszalin]], [[Poland]]
* [[Palencia]], [[Spain]]
* [[Peterborough]], [[United Kingdom]]

==External links==
