  <page>
    <title>Yuba County, California</title>
    <id>82133</id>
    <revision>
      <id>33491019</id>
      <timestamp>2006-01-01T17:06:02Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <username>Wbhpam</username>
        <id>695554</id>
      </contributor>
      <comment>/* Cities, towns, and communities */</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">{{Template:US County infobox|
 county  = Yuba County|
 state = California |
 seal = Yuba County ca seal.gif |
 map = California map showing Yuba County.png |
 map size = 225|
 founded = [[1850]] |
 seat = [[Marysville, California|Marysville]] | 
 area = 1,667 [[square kilometre|km&amp;sup2;]] (644 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]) |
 area water = 34 km&amp;sup2; (13 mi&amp;sup2;) |
 area percentage = 2.03% |
 census yr = 2000|
 pop = 60,219 |
 density = 37|
 web = www.co.yuba.ca.us|
|}}

'''Yuba County''' is located in the [[U.S. state]] of [[California]]'s [[California Central Valley|Central Valley]], north of [[Sacramento, California|Sacramento]], along the [[Feather River]].  As of [[2000]] its population is 60,219.  The [[county seat]] is [[Marysville, California|Marysville]].

==History==
Yuba County was one of the original counties of California, formed in [[1850]] at the time of statehood.  Parts of the county's territory were given to [[Placer County, California|Placer County]] in [[1851]], to [[Nevada County, California|Nevada County]] in [[1851]] and to [[Sierra County, California|Sierra County]] in [[1852]].

The county was named after the [[Yuba River]] by Captain [[John Sutter]] for the [[Native Americans in the United States|Native American]] village ''Yubu'', ''Yupu'' or ''Juba'' near the confluence of the Yuba and [[Feather River|Feather]] rivers. General [[Mariano Vallejo]] stated that the river was named ''Uba'' by an exploring expedition in [[1824]] because of the quantities of wild [[grapes]] (''uvas silvestres'' in [[Spanish language|Spanish]]) which they found growing on its banks.

== Geography ==
According to the [[United States Census Bureau|U.S. Census Bureau]], the county has a total area of 1,667 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (644 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  1,633 km&amp;sup2; (631 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 34 km&amp;sup2; (13 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is water.  The total area is 2.03% water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]][[Geographic references#2|&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;]] of [[2000]], there are 60,219 people, 20,535 households, and 14,805 families residing in the county.  The [[population density]] is 37/km&amp;sup2; (96/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 22,636 housing units at an average density of 14/km&amp;sup2; (36/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the county is 70.64% [[Race (U.S. census)|White]], 3.16% [[Race (U.S. census)|Black]] or [[Race (U.S. census)|African American]], 2.61% [[Race (U.S. census)|Native American]], 7.50% [[Race (U.S. census)|Asian]], 0.20% [[Race (U.S. census)|Pacific Islander]], 9.95% from [[race (U.S. census)|other races]], and 5.94% from two or more races.  17.35% of the population are [[Race (U.S. census)|Hispanic]] or [[Race (U.S. census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 20,535 households out of which 38.10% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 53.20% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 13.30% have a female householder with no husband present, and 27.90% are non-families. 21.70% of all households are made up of individuals and 8.20% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.87 and the average family size is 3.34.

In the county the population is spread out with 31.00% under the age of 18, 10.70% from 18 to 24, 28.00% from 25 to 44, 19.60% from 45 to 64, and 10.60% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 31 years.  For every 100 females there are 101.60 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 99.40 males.

The median income for a household in the county is $30,460, and the median income for a family is $34,103. Males have a median income of $27,845 versus $21,301 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the county is $14,124.  20.80% of the population and 16.30% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 27.60% of those under the age of 18 and 7.80% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

== Cities, towns, and communities ==
*[[Beale Air Force Base]]
*[[Camptonville, California | Camptonville]]
*[[Challenge-Brownsville, California|Challenge-Brownsville]]
*[[Linda, California|Linda]]
*[[Loma Rica, California|Loma Rica]]
*[[Marysville, California|Marysville]]
*[[Olivehurst, California|Olivehurst]]
*[[Plumas Lake, California|Plumas Lake]]
*[[Wheatland, California|Wheatland]]

==External link==
*[http://www.co.yuba.ca.us/ Yuba County Government website]

