  <page>
    <title>Hemera</title>
    <id>82137</id>
    <revision>
      <id>36369247</id>
      <timestamp>2006-01-23T16:03:12Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <ip>193.252.199.51</ip>
      </contributor>
      <text xml:space="preserve">In [[Greek mythology]], '''Hemera''' was a primordial goddess, born of [[Erebus]].  She was the goddess of the daytime.

Hemera's sister, [[Nyx]], was the goddess of the night.  Hemera left [[Tartarus]] just as Nyx entered it; when Hemera returned, Nyx left.

[[Thalassa]], the primordial sea goddess, was the daughter of Hemera and her brother, [[Aether]].

[[Category:Greek goddesses]][[Category:Solar goddesses]]

