  <page>
    <title>List of parishes of Louisiana</title>
    <id>82150</id>
    <revision>
      <id>33073451</id>
      <timestamp>2005-12-29T02:54:37Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <username>RJN</username>
        <id>681774</id>
      </contributor>
      <minor />
      <comment>Reverted commercial link spam</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">The [[U.S. state]] of [[Louisiana]] is divided into [[Parish (subnational entity)|parishes]] in the same way 
that the other states of the [[United States]] are divided into [[county|counties]]. 

==History==
In colonial Louisiana, which was officially [[Roman Catholic]] under both [[France]] and [[Spain]], civil government was centered on the ecclesiastical governing unit.

After the [[Louisiana Purchase]], Territorial Governor [[William C. C. Claiborne]] and his Legislative Council in [[1805]] divided [[Orleans Territory]] into twelve ''counties.'' Their boundaries were somewhat indefinite, but they generally coincided with the old church parishes, and kept the same names. In [[1807]], the territorial legislature passed an act dividing the territory into nineteen ''parishes'' &amp;mdash; but without abolishing the earlier twelve counties. For several years following this, both terms were used pretty much interchangeably. When a constitutional convention met in [[1811]] to prepare for Louisiana's admission as a state, they organized the state into seven judicial districts &amp;mdash; as groups of ''parishes''. The first official map of the state, in [[1816]], continued the use of the term, as did the revised Constitution of 1845. Louisiana's primary civil divisions have been officially known as ''parishes'' ever since.

== Alphabetical listing ==
[[Image:Louisiana parishes map.png|right|350px|Louisiana parishes]]
#[[Acadia Parish, Louisiana|Acadia Parish]] formed in 1886 from part of St. Landry Parish.
#[[Allen Parish, Louisiana|Allen Parish]] formed in 1912 from part of Calcasieu Parish.
#[[Ascension Parish, Louisiana|Ascension Parish]] One of the original 19 parishes formed in 1807.
#[[Assumption Parish, Louisiana|Assumption Parish]] One of the original 19 parishes formed in 1807.
#[[Avoyelles Parish, Louisiana|Avoyelles Parish]] One of the original 19 parishes formed in 1807.
#[[Beauregard Parish, Louisiana|Beauregard Parish]] formed in 1912 from part of Calcasieu Parish.
#[[Bienville Parish, Louisiana|Bienville Parish]] formed in 1848 from part of Claiborne Parish.
#[[Bossier Parish, Louisiana|Bossier Parish]] formed in 1843 from part Claiborne Parish.
#[[Caddo Parish, Louisiana|Caddo Parish]] formed in 1838 from part of Natchitoches Parish.
#[[Calcasieu Parish, Louisiana|Calcasieu Parish]] formed in 1840 from part of St. Landry Parish.
#[[Caldwell Parish, Louisiana|Caldwell Parish]] formed in 1838 from part of Catahoula Parish and Ouachita Parish.
#[[Cameron Parish, Louisiana|Cameron Parish]] formed in 1870 from parts of Calcasieu Parish and Vermilion Parish.
#[[Catahoula Parish, Louisiana|Catahoula Parish]] formed in 1808 from parts of Ouachita Parish and Rapides Parish.
#[[Claiborne Parish, Louisiana|Claiborne Parish]] formed in 1828 from part of Natchitoches Parish.
#[[Concordia Parish, Louisiana|Concordia Parish]] One of the original 19 parishes formed in 1807.
#[[De Soto Parish, Louisiana|De Soto Parish]] formed in 1843 from parts of Caddo Parish and Natchitoches Parish.
#[[East Baton Rouge Parish, Louisiana|East Baton Rouge Parish]] formed in 1810 from West Florida territory.
#[[East Carroll Parish, Louisiana|East Carroll Parish]] formed in 1877 when Carroll Parish was divided.
#[[East Feliciana Parish, Louisiana|East Feliciana Parish]] formed in 1824 when Feliciana Parish was divided.
#[[Evangeline Parish, Louisiana|Evangeline Parish]] formed in 1910 from part of St. Landry Parish.
#[[Franklin Parish, Louisiana|Franklin Parish]] formed in 1843 from parts of Carroll Parish, Catahoula Parish, Madison Parish and Ouachita Parish.
#[[Grant Parish, Louisiana|Grant Parish]] formed in 1869 from parts of Rapides Parish and Winn Parish.
#[[Iberia Parish, Louisiana|Iberia Parish]] formed in 1868 from parts of St. Martin Parish and St. Mary Parish.
#[[Iberville Parish, Louisiana|Iberville Parish]] One of the original 19 parishes formed in 1807.
#[[Jackson Parish, Louisiana|Jackson Parish]] formed in 1845 from parts of Claiborne Parish, Ouachita Parish and Union Parish.
#[[Jefferson Parish, Louisiana|Jefferson Parish]] formed in 1825 from part of Orleans Parish.
#[[Jefferson Davis Parish, Louisiana|Jefferson Davis Parish]] formed in 1912 from part of Calcasieu Parish.
#[[La Salle Parish, Louisiana|La Salle Parish]] formed in 1908 from part of Catahoula Parish.
#[[Lafayette Parish, Louisiana|Lafayette Parish]] formed in 1823 from part of St. Martin Parish.
#[[Lafourche Parish, Louisiana|Lafourche Parish]] One of the original 19 parishes formed in 1807. Was named Interior Parish until 1812 and Lafourche Interior Parish until 1853.
#[[Lincoln Parish, Louisiana|Lincoln Parish]] formed in 1873 from parts of Bienville Parish, Claiborne Parish, Jackson Parish and Union Parish.
#[[Livingston Parish, Louisiana|Livingston Parish]] formed in 1832 from part of St. Helena Parish.
#[[Madison Parish, Louisiana|Madison Parish]] formed in 1838 from Concordia Parish.
#[[Morehouse Parish, Louisiana|Morehouse Parish]] formed in 1844 from parts of Carroll Parish and Ouachita Parish.
#[[Natchitoches Parish, Louisiana|Natchitoches Parish]] One of the original 19 parishes formed in 1807.
#[[New Orleans, Louisiana|Orleans Parish]] One of the original 19 parishes formed in 1807. Today coterminous with the City of New Orleans.
#[[Ouachita Parish, Louisiana|Ouachita Parish]] One of the original 19 parishes formed in 1807.
#[[Plaquemines Parish, Louisiana|Plaquemines Parish]] One of the original 19 parishes formed in 1807.
#[[Pointe Coupee Parish, Louisiana|Pointe Coupee Parish]] One of the original 19 parishes formed in 1807.
#[[Rapides Parish, Louisiana|Rapides Parish]] One of the original 19 parishes formed in 1807.
#[[Red River Parish, Louisiana|Red River Parish]] formed in 1871 from parts of Bienville Parish, Bossier Parish, Caddo Parish and Natchitoches Parish.
#[[Richland Parish, Louisiana|Richland Parish]] formed in 1868 from parts of Carroll Parish, Franklin Parish, Morehouse Parish and Ouachita Parish.
#[[Sabine Parish, Louisiana|Sabine Parish]] formed in 1843 from parts of Caddo Parish and Natchitoches Parish.
#[[St. Bernard Parish, Louisiana|St. Bernard Parish]] One of the original 19 parishes formed in 1807.
#[[St. Charles Parish, Louisiana|St. Charles Parish]] One of the original 19 parishes formed in 1807.
#[[St. Helena Parish, Louisiana|St. Helena Parish]] formed in 1810 from West Florida territory.
#[[St. James Parish, Louisiana|St. James Parish]] One of the original 19 parishes formed in 1807.
#[[St. John the Baptist Parish, Louisiana|St. John the Baptist Parish]] One of the original 19 parishes formed in 1807.
#[[St. Landry Parish, Louisiana|St. Landry Parish]] One of the original 19 parishes formed in 1807.
#[[St. Martin Parish, Louisiana|St. Martin Parish]] One of the original 19 parishes formed in 1807.
#[[St. Mary Parish, Louisiana|St. Mary Parish]] formed in 1811 from part of St. Martin County.
#[[St. Tammany Parish, Louisiana|St. Tammany Parish]] formed in 1810 from West Florida territory.
#[[Tangipahoa Parish, Louisiana|Tangipahoa Parish]] formed in 1868 from parts of Livingston Parish, St. Helena Parish, St. Tammany Parish and Washington Parish.
#[[Tensas Parish, Louisiana|Tensas Parish]] formed in 1843 from part of Concordia Parish.
#[[Terrebonne Parish, Louisiana|Terrebonne Parish]] formed in 1822 from part of Lafourche Parish.
#[[Union Parish, Louisiana|Union Parish]] formed in 1839 from part of Ouachita Parish.
#[[Vermilion Parish, Louisiana|Vermilion Parish]] formed in 1844 from part of Lafayette Parish.
#[[Vernon Parish, Louisiana|Vernon Parish]] formed in 1871 from parts of Natchitoches Parish, Rapides Parish and Sabine Parish.
#[[Washington Parish, Louisiana|Washington Parish]] formed in 1819 from part of St. Tammany Parish.
#[[Webster Parish, Louisiana|Webster Parish]] formed in 1871 from parts of Bienville Parish, Bossier Parish and Claiborne Parish.
#[[West Baton Rouge Parish, Louisiana|West Baton Rouge Parish]] One of the original 19 parishes formed in 1807. Was named Baton Rouge Parish until 1812.
#[[West Carroll Parish, Louisiana|West Carroll Parish]] formed in 1877 when Carroll Parish was divided.
#[[West Feliciana Parish, Louisiana|West Feliciana Parish]] formed in 1824 when Feliciana Parish was divided.
#[[Winn Parish, Louisiana|Winn Parish]] formed in 1852 from parts of Catahoula Parish, Natchitoches Parish and Rapides Parish.

== Defunct Parishes ==

#[[Biloxi Parish, Louisiana|Biloxi Parish]] formed in 1811 from West Florida territory. Eliminated in 1812 when part of West Florida was transferred to Mississippi Territory.
#[[Carroll Parish, Louisiana|Carroll Parish]] formed in 1838 from part of Ouachita Parish. Divided in 1877 into East Carroll Parish and West Carroll Parish.
#[[Feliciana Parish, Louisiana|Feliciana Parish]] formed in 1810 from West Florida territory. Divided in 1824 into East Feliciana Parish and West Feliciana Parish.
#[[Pascagoula Parish, Louisiana|Pascagoula Parish]] formed in 1811 from West Florida territory. Eliminated in 1812 when part of West Florida was transferred to Mississippi Territory.
#[[Warren Parish, Louisiana|Warren Parish]] formed in 1811 from part of Concordia Parish. Merged into Concordia Parish and Ouachita Parish in 1814.

== Counties (1805-45) ==
#[[Acadia County, Louisiana|Acadia County]]
#[[Attakapas County, Louisiana|Attakapas County]]
#[[Concordia County, Louisiana|Concordia County]]
#[[Feliciana County, Louisiana|Feliciana County]] established in 1810 from West Florida territory.
#[[German Coast County, Louisiana|German Coast County]]
#[[Iberville County, Louisiana|Iberville County]]
#[[Lafourche County, Louisiana|Lafourche County]]
#[[Natchitoches County, Louisiana|Natchitoches County]]
#[[Opelousas County, Louisiana|Opelousas County]]
#[[Orleans County, Louisiana|Orleans County]]
#[[Ouachita County, Louisiana|Ouachita County]]
#[[Pointe Coupee County, Louisiana|Pointe Coupee County]]
#[[Rapides County, Louisiana|Rapides County]]

== Fictional Parishes ==
In the [[novel]] ''[[A Confederacy of Dunces]]'', author [[John Kennedy Toole]] created the fictional &quot;St. Odo of Cluny Parish&quot;.

