      <text xml:space="preserve">'''List of [[Pennsylvania]] counties:'''
[[Image:Pennsylvania-counties-map.gif|thumb|Pennsylvania counties]]
#[[Adams County, Pennsylvania|Adams County]], formed in 1800 from parts of York County.  County seat: [[Gettysburg, Pennsylvania|Gettysburg]].
#[[Allegheny County, Pennsylvania|Allegheny County]], formed in 1788 from parts of Washington and Westmoreland Counties. County seat: [[Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania|Pittsburgh]].
#[[Armstrong County, Pennsylvania|Armstrong County]], formed in 1800 from parts of Allegheny, Lycoming, and Westmoreland Counties.  County seat: [[Kittanning, Pennsylvania|Kittanning]].
#[[Beaver County, Pennsylvania|Beaver County]], formed in 1800 from parts of Allegheny and Washington Counties.  County seat: [[Beaver, Pennsylvania|Beaver]].
#[[Bedford County, Pennsylvania|Bedford County]], formed in 1771 from parts of Cumberland County.  County seat: [[Bedford, Pennsylvania|Bedford]].
#[[Berks County, Pennsylvania|Berks County]], formed in 1752 from parts of Chester, Lancaster and Philadelphia Counties.  County seat: [[Reading, Pennsylvania|Reading]].
#[[Blair County, Pennsylvania|Blair County]], formed in 1846 from parts of Huntingdon and Bedford Counties.  County seat: [[Hollidaysburg, Pennsylvania|Hollidaysburg]].
#[[Bradford County, Pennsylvania|Bradford County]], formed in 1810 from parts of Luzerne and Lycoming Counties; originally called Ontario County, renamed as Bradford County in 1812. County seat: [[Towanda, Pennsylvania|Towanda]].
#[[Bucks County, Pennsylvania|Bucks County]], one of the original counties at the formation of Pennsylvania in 1682.  County seat: [[Doylestown, Pennsylvania|Doylestown]].
#[[Butler County, Pennsylvania|Butler County]], formed in 1800 from parts of Allegheny County.  County seat: [[Butler, Pennsylvania|Butler]].
#[[Cambria County, Pennsylvania|Cambria County]], formed in 1804 from parts of Somerset and Huntingdon Counties. County seat: [[Ebensburg, Pennsylvania|Ebensburg]].
#[[Cameron County, Pennsylvania|Cameron County]], formed in 1860 from parts of Clinton, Elk, McKean, and Potter Counties. County seat: [[Emporium, Pennsylvania|Emporium]].
#[[Carbon County, Pennsylvania|Carbon County]], formed in 1843 from parts of Monroe and Northampton Counties. County seat: [[Jim Thorpe, Pennsylvania|Jim Thorpe]].
#[[Centre County, Pennsylvania|Centre County]], formed in 1800 from parts of Lycoming, Mifflin, Northumberland, and Huntingdon Counties. County seat: [[Bellefonte, Pennsylvania|Bellefonte]].
#[[Chester County, Pennsylvania|Chester County]], one of the original counties at the formation of Pennsylvania in 1682. County seat: [[West Chester, Pennsylvania|West Chester]].
#[[Clarion County, Pennsylvania|Clarion County]], formed in 1839 from parts of Venango and Armstrong Counties.  County seat: [[Clarion, Pennsylvania|Clarion]].	
#[[Clearfield County, Pennsylvania|Clearfield County]], formed in 1804 from parts of Lycoming and Huntingdon Counties; Clearfield functioned as a part of Centre County for judiciary purposes until 1822. County seat: [[Clearfield, Pennsylvania|Clearfield]].
#[[Clinton County, Pennsylvania|Clinton County]], formed in 1839 from parts of Lycoming and Centre Counties. County seat: [[Lock Haven, Pennsylvania|Lock Haven]].
#[[Columbia County, Pennsylvania|Columbia County]], formed in 1813 from parts of Northumberland and Luzerne Counties. County seat: [[Bloomsburg, Pennsylvania|Bloomsburg]].
#[[Crawford County, Pennsylvania|Crawford County]], formed in 1800 from parts of Allegheny County. County seat: [[Meadville, Pennsylvania|Meadville]].
#[[Cumberland County, Pennsylvania|Cumberland County]], formed in 1750 from parts of Lancaster County. County seat: [[Carlisle, Pennsylvania|Carlisle]].
#[[Dauphin County, Pennsylvania|Dauphin County]], formed in 1785 from parts of Lancaster County. County seat: [[Harrisburg, Pennsylvania|Harrisburg]].
#[[Delaware County, Pennsylvania|Delaware County]], formed in 1789 from parts of Chester County. County seat: [[Media, Pennsylvania|Media]].
#[[Elk County, Pennsylvania|Elk County]], formed 1843 from parts of Jefferson, McKean and Clearfield Counties. County seat: [[Ridgway, Pennsylvania|Ridgway]].
#[[Erie County, Pennsylvania|Erie County]], formed in 1800 from parts of Allegheny County; attached to Crawford County until 1803. County seat: [[Erie, Pennsylvania|Erie]].
#[[Fayette County, Pennsylvania|Fayette County]], formed in 1783 from parts of Westmoreland County. County seat: [[Uniontown, Pennsylvania|Uniontown]].
#[[Forest County, Pennsylvania|Forest County]], formed in 1848 from parts of Jefferson County; attached to Jefferson County until 1857. County seat: [[Tionesta, Pennsylvania|Tionesta]].
#[[Franklin County, Pennsylvania|Franklin County]], formed in 1784 from parts of Cumberland County. County seat: [[Chambersburg, Pennsylvania|Chambersburg]].
#[[Fulton County, Pennsylvania|Fulton County]], formed in 1850 from parts of Bedford County. County seat: [[McConnellsburg, Pennsylvania|McConnellsburg]]
#[[Greene County, Pennsylvania|Greene County]], formed in 1796 from parts of Washington County. County seat: [[Waynesburg, Pennsylvania|Waynesburg]]
#[[Huntingdon County, Pennsylvania|Huntingdon County]], formed in 1787 from parts of Bedford County. County seat: [[Huntingdon, Pennsylvania|Huntingdon]].
#[[Indiana County, Pennsylvania|Indiana County]], formed in 1803 from parts of Lycoming and Westmoreland Counties; it was attached to Westmoreland County until 1806. County seat: [[Indiana, Pennsylvania|Indiana]].
#[[Jefferson County, Pennsylvania|Jefferson County]], formed in 1804 from parts of Lycoming County. Attached to Westmoreland County until 1806 and to Indiana County until 1830. County seat: [[Brookville, Pennsylvania|Brookville]].
#[[Juniata County, Pennsylvania|Juniata County]], formed 1831 from parts of Mifflin County. County seat: [[Mifflintown, Pennsylvania|Mifflintown]].
#[[Lackawanna County, Pennsylvania|Lackawanna County]], formed in 1878 from parts of Luzerne County. County seat: [[Scranton, Pennsylvania|Scranton]].
#[[Lancaster County, Pennsylvania|Lancaster County]], formed in 1729 from parts of Chester County. County seat: [[Lancaster, Pennsylvania|Lancaster]].
#[[Lawrence County, Pennsylvania|Lawrence County]], formed in 1849 from parts of Beaver and Mercer Counties. County seat: [[New Castle, Pennsylvania|New Castle]].
#[[Lebanon County, Pennsylvania|Lebanon County]], fourmed in 1813 from parts of Dauphin and Lancaster Counties. County seat: [[Lebanon, Pennsylvania|Lebanon]].
#[[Lehigh County, Pennsylvania|Lehigh County]], formed in 1812 from parts of Northampton County. County seat: [[Allentown, Pennsylvania|Allentown]].
#[[Luzerne County, Pennsylvania|Luzerne County]], formed in 1786 from parts of Northumberland County. County seat: [[Wilkes-Barre, Pennsylvania|Wilkes-Barre]].
#[[Lycoming County, Pennsylvania|Lycoming County]], formed in 1795 from parts of Northumberland County. County seat: [[Williamsport, Pennsylvania|Williamsport]].
#[[McKean County, Pennsylvania|McKean County]], formed in 1804 from parts of Lycoming County; Attached to Centre County until 1814 and to Lycoming County until 1826 for judicial and elective purposes. McKean was fully organized only in 1826. County seat: [[Smethport, Pennsylvania|Smethport]].
#[[Mercer County, Pennsylvania|Mercer County]], formed in 1800 from parts of Allegheny County. County seat: [[Mercer, Pennsylvania|Mercer]].
#[[Mifflin County, Pennsylvania|Mifflin County]], formed in 1789 from parts of Cumberland and Northumberland Counties. County seat: [[Lewistown, Pennsylvania|Lewistown]].
#[[Monroe County, Pennsylvania|Monroe County]], formed in 1836 from parts of Pike and Northampton Counties. County seat: [[Stroudsburg, Pennsylvania|Stroudsburg]].
#[[Montgomery County, Pennsylvania|Montgomery County]], formed in 1784 from parts of Philadelphia County. County seat: [[Norristown, Pennsylvania|Norristown]].
#[[Montour County, Pennsylvania|Montour County]], formed in 1850 from parts of Columbia County. County seat: [[Danville, Pennsylvania|Danville]].
#[[Northampton County, Pennsylvania|Northampton County]], formed in 1752 from parts of Bucks County. County seat: [[Easton, Pennsylvania|Easton]].
#[[Northumberland County, Pennsylvania|Northumberland County]], formed in 1772 from parts of Lancaster, Berks, Bedford, Cumberland, and Northampton Counties. County seat: [[Sunbury, Pennsylvania|Sunbury]].
#[[Perry County, Pennsylvania|Perry County]], formed in 1820 from parts of Cumberland County. County seat: [[New Bloomfield, Pennsylvania|New Bloomfield]].
#[[Philadelphia County, Pennsylvania|Philadelphia County]], one of the original counties at the formation of [[Pennsylvania]] in 1682. The city and county of Philadelphia were combined in 1854 and city and county offices merged in 1952.
#[[Pike County, Pennsylvania|Pike County]], formed in 1814 from parts of Wayne County.  County seat: [[Milford, Pennsylvania|Milford]].
#[[Potter County, Pennsylvania|Potter County]], Formed in 1804 from Lycoming county. Attached to Lycoming County until 18265 and to McKean County until 1835 for judicial purposes, Potter was not fully organized until 1835. County seat: [[Coudersport, Pennsylvania|Coudersport]].
#[[Schuylkill County, Pennsylvania|Schuylkill County]], formed in 1811 from parts of Berks and Northampton Counties.  County seat: [[Pottsville, Pennsylvania|Pottsville]].
#[[Snyder County, Pennsylvania|Snyder County]], formed in 1855 from parts of Union County. County seat: [[Middleburg, Pennsylvania|Middleburg]].
#[[Somerset County, Pennsylvania|Somerset County]], formed in 1795 from parts of Bedford County.  County seat: [[Somerset, Pennsylvania|Somerset]].
#[[Sullivan County, Pennsylvania|Sullivan County]], formed in 1847 from parts of Lycoming County; attached to Lycoming until 1848.  County seat: [[Laporte, Pennsylvania|Laporte]].
#[[Susquehanna County, Pennsylvania|Susquehanna County]], formed in 1810 from parts of Luzerne County ; attached to Luzerne County until 1812. County seat: [[Montrose, Pennsylvania|Montrose]].
#[[Tioga County, Pennsylvania|Tioga County]], formed in 1804 from parts of Lycoming County; attached to Lycoming until 1812. County seat: [[Wellsboro, Pennsylvania|Wellsboro]].
#[[Union County, Pennsylvania|Union County]], formed in 1813 from parts of Northumberland County. County seat: [[Lewisburg, Pennsylvania|Lewisburg]].
#[[Venango County, Pennsylvania|Venango County]], formed in 1800 from parts of Allegheny and Lycoming Counties; attached to until 1805. County seat: [[Franklin, Pennsylvania|Franklin]].
#[[Warren County, Pennsylvania|Warren County]], formed in 1800 from parts of Allegheny and Lycoming counties; attached to Crawford County until 1805 and then to Venango until Warren was formally organized in 1819. County seat: [[Warren, Pennsylvania|Warren]].
#[[Washington County, Pennsylvania|Washington County]], formed in 1781 from parts of Westmoreland County. County seat: [[Washington, Pennsylvania|Washington]].
#[[Wayne County, Pennsylvania|Wayne County]], formed in 1798 from parts of Northampton County. County seat: [[Honesdale, Pennsylvania|Honesdale]].
#[[Westmoreland County, Pennsylvania|Westmoreland County]], formed in 1773 from parts of Bedford County. County seat: [[Greensburg, Pennsylvania|Greensburg]].
#[[Wyoming County, Pennsylvania|Wyoming County]], formed in 1842 from parts of Luzerne County. County seat: [[Tunkhannock, Pennsylvania|Tunkhannock]].
#[[York County, Pennsylvania|York County]], formed in 1749 from parts of Lancaster County. County seat: [[York, Pennsylvania|York]].

[http://quickfacts.census.gov/qfd/maps/pennsylvania_map.html map]

