  <page>
    <title>Martinair</title>
    <id>82209</id>
    <revision>
      <id>39743886</id>
      <timestamp>2006-02-15T15:40:09Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <username>Carabinieri</username>
        <id>389283</id>
      </contributor>
      <comment>/* Services */ dab [[San Felipe de Puerto Plata]]</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">[[image:martinair.arp.750pix.jpg|thumb|right|250px| Martinair aircraft at Amsterdam (Schiphol) Airport, the Netherlands (two McDonnell Douglas MD-11 and a Boeing 747)]]

'''Martinair''' is both a charter and scheduled [[airline]] based in the [[Netherlands]], with daily passenger or cargo charter and regular flights to many destinations around the world from its main base of [[Schiphol International Airport]] (AMS) near [[Amsterdam]]. 

Martinair occasionally flies certain flights instead of [[KLM]]. Martinair also flies some destinations full time with KLM code. The airline has hubs at [[Sharjah International Airport]] (SHJ), [[Hong Kong International Airport]] (HKG) and [[Miami International Airport]] (MIA).

== Code Data ==
*[[International Air Transport Association|IATA]] Code: '''MP'''
*[[International Civil Aviation Organisation|ICAO]] Code: '''MPH'''
*Callsign: '''Martinair'''

== History ==
* The airline was founded on [[24 May]] [[1958]] as Martin's Air Charter (MAC), by J. Martin Schröder, with one plane. 
* In [[1963]] Mr. Schröder sold 49% of the company to four equal shipping company shareholders (12.25% each, Nedlloyd would wind up one of them). KLM would later purchase the 50+% that Mr. Schröder owned, buying him out. 
* The name was changed to Martinair Holland, from MAC in [[1966]]. 
* A healthy boost came in [[1967]] with the opening of business to the [[United States]]. 
* Martinair becomes all jet-powered in [[1971]]. 
* Tragedy struck when a Martinair [[DC-8]] on landing approach to [[Colombo]], [[Sri Lanka]] flew into the side of a mountain on [[4 December]] [[1974]], killing 184 Indonesian passengers and 7 Dutch crew members. 
* [[1991]], the first aircraft with the ''&quot;Martinair Cargo&quot;'' name is introduced, and the ''&quot;Holland&quot;'' is dropped from all aircraft. 
* The company's second crash occurred at [[Faro, Portugal|Faro]] [[Portugal]] when a [[DC-10]] crashed [[21 December]] [[1992]], killing 56 people (including 2 crew members), out of 340 people on board. 
* Martinair buys a 40% stake in [[Colombia|Colombian]] cargo carrier [[TAMPA Cargo]], based in [[Medellín]], in [[1996]].  
* Martinair President &amp; CEO Martin Schröder retires from day-to-day activities with the company in [[1998]]. Also that year, the European Commission in Brussels refused KLM's offer to purchase Nedlloyd's shares, which would have made KLM the sole-owner. 
* In [[2003]] the company increased its stake in TAMPA Cargo, becoming Tampa's majority shareholder.

== Structure ==
* Owned by KLM (50%) and [[P&amp;O Nedlloyd]] (50%)
* Has a 50+% ownership holding of [[TAMPA Cargo]]
* 3,490 employees

== Subsidiaries ==
* Martinair Flying School
* Martinair Food (Marfo - airline meal service provider)
* Martinair Partyservice (special events catering services)
* Martinair Promotions (hostess product demonstrations/greeting @ seminars, conferences, business events, expositions, &amp; VIP receptions)
* Skyjob (temporary employment agency, flying courses, occupational health &amp; safety services, promotional activities).

== Services ==
International scheduled services (as of July 2005): [[Calgary, Alberta|Calgary]], [[Cancún]], [[Colombo]], [[Edmonton, Alberta|Edmonton]], [[Havana]], [[Holguin]], [[Kingston, Jamaica|Kingston]], [[Malé]], [[Miami]], [[Montego Bay]], [[Orlando, Florida|Orlando]], [[Isla Margarita|Porlamar]], [[Punta Cana]]/[[San Felipe de Puerto Plata|Puerto Plata]]/[[Santo Domingo]], [[San José, Costa Rica|San José]], [[Scarborough, Tobago|Scarborough]], [[Toronto]], [[Vancouver]] and [[Varadero]].

Martinair also operates charter flights inside Europe and North Africa with single class Airbus A320 aircraft, and in peak times converts one or two of its McDonnell Douglas MD-11 aircraft to carry extra passengers.

The largest scheduled block of flights is Martinair's freight operation, utilising MD-11 and Boeing 747 aircraft, operating scheduled freight flights worldwide.

== Fleet ==
The Martinair fleet consists of the following aircraft (at April 2005):

*3 [[Airbus A320|Airbus A320-200]]
*1 [[Boeing 737|Boeing 737-800]]
*4 [[Boeing 747|Boeing 747-200]]
*5 [[Boeing 767|Boeing 767-300]]
*7 [[McDonnell Douglas MD-11]]
*1 [[Dornier Do 228|Dornier 228-212]]
*1 [[Fokker F70|Fokker 70]]

==External links==
* [http://www.martinair.com/ Martinair]
* [http://www.planemad.net/Airline/NL/Martinair_Holland_(MP_MPH)/Fleet.htm?show=all Martinair Fleet Detail]
* [http://www.airlinequality.com/Forum/martinair.htm Martinair Passenger Opinions]
* [http://www.martinaircargo.com/ Martinair Cargo]
* [http://www.tampacargo.com/Tampa_Cargo/inicio.htm Tampa Cargo (Spanish)]
* [http://www.tampacargo.com/Tampa_Ingles/inicio_ing.htm Tampa Cargo (English)]

[[Category:Airlines of the Netherlands]]
{{airlistbox}}
[[de:Martinair]]
[[fr:Martinair Holland]]
[[nl:Martinair]]</text>
