*[[American Broadcasting Company|ABC]] (American Broadcasting Company) - based in [[United States|USA]], but also broadcasts into [[Canada]] and [[Mexico]], and parts of the [[Caribbean]]. It operates the [[Freeview]] channel [[abc1]] in the [[United Kingdom]].
*[[ANT1]] - Greek language, broadcasts into [[Republic of Macedonia|Macedonia]], [[Albania]], parts of [[Italy]], and [[Turkey]], broadcasts worldwide (mostly).
*[[Australian Broadcasting Corporation|ABC Asia Pacific]] (Australian Broadcasting Corporation) - based in Australia, broadcasting to the neighbouring region.
*[[American Forces Network|AFN]] American Forces Network, broadcasts worldwide via satellite, only available to US Forces and their families, but is available in South Korea. 
*[[Al Jazeera]] - based in [[Qatar]], Arabic language
*[[Abu Dhabi TV]] - Worldwide Arabic-language channel
*[[BBC]] - British Broadcasting Corporation, based in the United Kingdom. operating [[BBC World]] news and information service, [[BBC Prime]] and [[BBC Food]] general entertainment and lifestyle services in Europe, the Middle East, Africa  and North America [[BBC America]], [[BBC Canada]], [[BBC Japan]] and [[BBC Kids]].) 
*[[British Forces Broadcasting Service|BFBS]] - British Forces Broadcasting Service, operating BFBS Television in Germany, Cyprus, former Yugoslavia, Iraq, Falkland Islands, Belize- only available to HM Forces and their families, except in Falkland Islands.
*[[British Satellite Broadcasting]]
*[[Cartoon Network]] Cartoons  
*[[Canadian Broadcasting Corporation|CBC]] - based in [[Canada]], but also broadcast into part of [[United States|USA]], [[Bermuda]] and probably [[Greenland]].
*[[CBS]] - based in [[United States|USA]], but also broadcasts into [[Canada]], [[Mexico]], and parts of the [[Caribbean]].   
