      <text xml:space="preserve">[[Image:Kourou corv 673.jpg|200px|thumb|right|Kourou]]
'''Kourou''' is a town and [[commune in France|commune]] in [[French Guiana]], some 40 km northwest of the capital [[Cayenne]] at the mouth of the [[Kourou river]] on the [[Atlantic]] coast. It has a population of 20,000, many of whom are Metropolitan [[French people|French]], earning Kourou the nickname 'White City.' The ''[[Centre Spatial Guyanais]]'' (Guiana Space Centre), where the [[European Space Agency]] starts missions, is located outside the town. Kourou was formerly a [[prison colony]]: see [[Devil's Island]].
Part of the town is closed during [[rocket launch]].
[[Image:Kourou_rain_pluie.jpg|200px|thumb|left|Kourou's ''Bois Chaudat'' lake during the rainy season.]]

