    <title>Merneferre Ai</title>
    <id>82360</id>
    <revision>
      <id>40342666</id>
      <timestamp>2006-02-19T23:04:32Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <username>That Guy, From That Show!</username>
        <id>419920</id>
      </contributor>
      <minor />
      <comment>[[WP:AWB|AWB assisted]] removed redundant category &amp; cleanup formatting</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">Birth name: '''Ai'''

Throne name: '''Mernefere''' 

'''Merneferre Ai''' was an [[Ancient Egypt]]ian ruler of the [[Thirteenth dynasty of Egypt]]. He reigned around [[1720s BC|1720 BC]]. Following the [[Turin King List]] he ruled for 23 years. He is mainly known from many [[scarab]] seals. In the Delta there was found a [[Pyramidion|pyramidion]] with his name. He is the last Egyptian king of the 13th Dynasty known from objects found in Lower and Upper Egypt, indicating that he still ruled most parts of the country. 

This [[pharaoh]] is also known as '''Aya''' or '''Eje'''.

He is sometimes confused with [[Ay|Kheperkheprure Ai]], a ruler at the end of the [[Eighteenth dynasty of Egypt|18th Dynasty]].

{{Pharaoh | Prev=[[Wahibre Ibiau]] | Dynasty=[[Thirteenth dynasty of Egypt|Thirteenth Dynasty]] | Next=[[Neferhotep II]]}}

[[Category:Pharaohs]]

[[de:Aja I.]]


{{Ancient-Egypt-stub}}</text>
